{"id": "21", "question": "magellan of virginia provider", "gt": "Magellan of Virginia is the Behavioral Health Services Administrator for the Virginia Department of Medical Assistance Services. They administer behavioral health services for members enrolled in Virginia’s Medicaid and FAMIS programs. The site is also for providers, offering them resources like weekly Q&A sessions each Friday from 1 p.m. - 2:30 p.m. where they can address their questions and issues. Additionally, they offer continuing education clock hours/credits for e-learning courses, approved by organizations like the American Psychological Association and the Association of Social Work Boards.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, Magellan of Virginia is a behavioral health services provider administering services for Virginia Medicaid and FAMIS program enrollees, hosting weekly Provider Q&A Sessions on Fridays from 1 p.m. to 2:30 p.m. open to all providers, and ensuring quality behavioral health services are delivered to Virginia Medicaid enrollees through partnerships with members, providers, and stakeholders to elevate healthcare delivery quality and satisfaction while improving Virginians' overall health and well-being.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, Magellan of Virginia is a behavioral health services provider administering services for Virginia Medicaid and FAMIS program enrollees, hosting weekly Provider Q&A Sessions on Fridays from 1 p.m. to 2:30 p.m. open to all providers, and ensuring quality behavioral health services are delivered to Virginia Medicaid enrollees through partnerships with members, providers, and stakeholders to elevate healthcare delivery quality and satisfaction while improving Virginians' overall health and well-being.", "time_sec": 8.015, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video