{"id": "22", "question": "magellan of virginia provider", "gt": "Magellan of Virginia is a provider of behavioral health services for members enrolled in Virginia's Medicaid and FAMIS programs. They ensure the delivery of quality behavioral health services to Virginia Medicaid enrollees and work towards improving the overall health and well-being of Virginians. They also offer continuing education clock hours/credits for e-learning courses and host weekly Q&A sessions for providers to address their questions and issues.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, Magellan of Virginia is a behavioral health services provider administering services for Virginia Medicaid and FAMIS program enrollees, hosting weekly Provider Q&A Sessions on Fridays from 1 p.m. to 2:30 p.m. open to all providers, and ensuring quality behavioral health services are delivered to Virginia Medicaid enrollees through partnerships with members, providers, and stakeholders to elevate healthcare delivery quality and satisfaction while improving Virginians' overall health and well-being.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, Magellan of Virginia is a behavioral health services provider administering services for Virginia Medicaid and FAMIS program enrollees, hosting weekly Provider Q&A Sessions on Fridays from 1 p.m. to 2:30 p.m. open to all providers, and ensuring quality behavioral health services are delivered to Virginia Medicaid enrollees through partnerships with members, providers, and stakeholders to elevate healthcare delivery quality and satisfaction while improving Virginians' overall health and well-being.", "time_sec": 7.988, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 35957, 1408, 1278, 4265, 42679, 1044, 7724, 64762, 1307, 1