{"id": "38", "question": "how to cook pollock?", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's how to cook pollock:\n\nPreheat the oven to 350°F (175°C). Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper. Place the fillets on a baking sheet lined with parchment paper or aluminum foil. You can also add sliced onions, green peppers, and tomatoes on top of the fillets. Bake for 15 minutes or until the fish flakes easily with a fork. If desired, top with cheese and return to the oven for an additional 3 minutes or until the cheese is melted.\n\nTherefore, the answer is not \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\"", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to cook pollock: 1 Preheat oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C). 2 Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper. 3 Place on a baking sheet sprayed with butter flavored cooking spray and layer with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices. 4 Bake in preheated oven until fish has cooked and flakes easily, about 15 minutes. 5 Turn oven off, place two slices of cheese on each fillet. 6 Return fish to the oven and allow cheese to melt, about 3 minutes.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to cook pollock: 1 Preheat oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C). 2 Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper. 3 Place on a baking sheet sprayed with butter flavored cooking spray and layer with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices. 4 Bake in preheated oven until fish has cooked and flakes easily, about 15 minutes. 5 Turn oven off, place two slices of cheese on each fillet. 6 Return fish to the oven and allow cheese to melt, about 3 minutes.", "time_sec": 9.923, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 35957, 1408, 1278, 4265, 42679, 1044, 