{"id": "43", "question": "how to get plastic out of clothes dryer", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is how to get plastic out of a clothes dryer:\n\n1. Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic.\n2. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, taking care not to damage the dryer's interior.\n3. Apply 1 to 2 tsp. nail polish remover to a clean cloth, and rub the plastic to dissolve it. Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover.\n4. Mix 1 tsp. liquid laundry soap with 1 cup water. Dip a clean cloth in this solution, and rub the area again. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.\n\nIf the plastic is still difficult to remove, you can try heating it with a hair dryer or heat gun before attempting to scrape it off. However, if the plastic cannot be removed completely, it may be necessary to replace the drum or the entire dryer.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to get plastic out of a clothes dryer: Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, taking care not to damage the dryer's interior. Apply 1 to 2 tsp. nail polish remover to a clean cloth, and rub the plastic to dissolve it. Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover. Mix 1 tsp. liquid laundry soap with 1 cup water. Dip a clean cloth in this solution, and rub the area again. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water. If the plastic is extremely difficult to remove, heat it with a hair dryer or heat gun, then attempt to peel it off; if unsuccessful, replace the drum or the entire dryer, and call a service technician for drum replacement.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to get plastic out of a clothes dryer: Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, taking care not to damage the dryer's interior. Apply 1 to 2 tsp. nail polish remover to a clean cloth, and rub the plastic to dissolve it. Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover. Mix 1 tsp. liquid laundry soap with 1 cup water. Dip a clean cloth in this solution, and rub the area again. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water. If the plastic is extremely difficult to remove, heat it with a hair dryer or heat gun, then attempt to peel it off; if unsuccessful, replace the drum or the entire dryer, and call a service technician for drum replacement.", "time_sec": 14.327, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 35957, 1408, 1278, 4265, 42679, 1044, 1317, 2012, 17985, 1848, 1307, 1261, 23702, 129544, 1058, 15614, 1278, 129544, 1408, 1261, 8385, 9436, 1394, 1032, 1050, 1048, 7334, 1317, 6444, 1262, 1278, 17985, 1046, 4167, 118505, 1278, 17985, 2490, 1454, 1261, 32656, 1505, 17985, 14260, 4427, 1505, 15504, 55941, 1569, 1044, 8198, 3831, 1605, 1317, 10605, 1278, 129544, 1681, 14772, 1046, 63882, 1032, 1049, 1317, 1032, 1050, 1257, 2308, 1046, 61122, 2223, 2140, 2357, 3245, 1317, 1261, 9375, 18473, 1044, 1321, 13523, 1278, 17985, 1317, 89736, 1494, 1046, 17922, 1278, 4457, 1454, 1261, 49922, 18473, 1317, 38124, 1415, 1278, 61122, 2223, 2140, 2357, 3245, 1046, 28978, 1032, 1049, 1257, 2308, 1046, 11301, 84603, 50584, 1454, 1032, 1049, 19339, 4180, 1046, 53196, 1261, 9375, 18473, 1294, 1593, 5097, 1044, 1321, 13523, 1278, 4457, 2790, 1046, 65117, 1415, 2903, 1454, 1261, 18473, 103387, 1294, 9375, 4180, 1046, 3367, 1278, 17985, 1395, 16843, 6593, 1317, 8559, 1044, 9374, 1494, 1454, 1261, 10188, 129544, 1505, 9374, 15640, 1044, 2430, 6983, 1317, 116439, 1494, 2490, 1059, 1693, 52249, 1044, 14422, 1278, 27989, 15