{"id": "59", "question": "how can i keep birds from building a nest on my porch", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here are some ways to keep birds from building nests on your porch:\n\n1. Attach bird netting to the eaves around the perimeter of your porch with a staple gun (Passage 1:4). This will prevent birds from reaching the areas they often choose to build their nests.\n2. Install bird netting over the top of the light fixture to block the birds' access to it (Passage 2:1). Choose a non-flammable netting that is safe to use around light bulbs, and ensure that it is installed so that it doesn't entangle birds.\n3. Mount a plastic hawk on or near your porch to scare the birds from the area (Passage 3:1). Move the plastic hawk periodically to avoid the birds becoming accustomed to it.\n\nPlease note that the effectiveness of these methods may vary depending on the type of birds and the location of your porch. If the above methods do not work, you may need to consider other solutions or consult with a professional for assistance.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, you can keep birds from building a nest on your porch by attaching bird netting to the eves around the perimeter of your porch with a staple gun, or to the top of the porch if it has open rafters, and by installing nonflammable bird netting over the top of light fixtures to block access, ensuring it is installed to avoid entangling birds, or by mounting a plastic hawk on or near your porch and moving it periodically to prevent birds from becoming accustomed to it, as bird nests can block ventilation systems, are made from flammable materials, and bird droppings can transmit disease.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, you can keep birds from building a nest on your porch by attaching bird netting to the eves around the perimeter of your porch with a staple gun, or to the top o