{"id": "75", "question": "how to cook brats", "gt": "Based on the passages provided, the steps to cook brats are as follows:\n\n1. Prick the bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding as they cook. \n2. Combine beer and onions in a large pot and bring it to a boil. Submerge the bratwurst in the beer, adding red pepper flakes, garlic powder, salt, and pepper.\n3. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\n4. In the meantime, preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat and lightly oil the grate.\n5. After simmering, remove the bratwurst from the beer mixture and reduce the heat to low, continuing to cook the onions.\n6. Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill, turning occasionally, for about 10 to 14 minutes until they are browned evenly.\n7. Serve the bratwurst with the beer and onion mixture as a topping or side.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, here is how to cook brats: 1 Prick bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding as they cook. 2 Place bratwurst in a large stock pot with onions, butter, and beer. 3 Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes. 4 Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat. 5 Lightly oil the grill grate. 6 Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill for 10 to 14 minutes, turning occasionally to brown evenly. 7 Reduce heat to medium and cook another 10 to 12 minutes. 8 Remove the bratwurst from the beer mixture; reduce heat to low, and continue cooking the onions. 9 Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill, turning once, 5 to 10 minutes. 10 Serve with the beer mixture as a topping or side.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, here is how to cook brats: 1 Prick bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding as they cook. 2 Place bratwurst in a large stock pot with onions, butter, and beer. 3 Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes. 4 Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat. 5 Lightly oil the grill grate. 6 Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill for 10 to 14 minutes, turning occasionally to brown evenly. 7 Reduce heat to medium and cook another 10 to 12 minutes. 8 Remove the bratwurst from the beer mixture; reduce heat to low, and continue cooking the onions. 9 Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill, turning once, 5 to 10 minutes. 10 Serve with the beer mixture as a topping or side.", "time_sec": 15.911, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 35957, 1408, 1278, 4265, 42679, 1044, 3226, 1395, 2606, 1317, 17966, 2795, 2476, 1058, 1032, 1049, 3216, 1985, 87016, 1119, 108277, 1454, 1261, 40191, 1317, 7495, 2424, 1562, 3543, 7967, 1435, 2127, 17966, 1046, 1032, 1050, 22435, 87016, 1119, 108277, 1294, 1261, 4329, 12169, 3418, 1454, 126255, 1044, 34262, 1044, 1321, 34568, 1046, 1032, 1051, 22435, 1278, 3418, 2136, 9566, 9374, 1321, 2500, 2221, 1394, 1032, 1049, 1053, 1317, 1032, 1050, 1048, 7334, 1046, 1032, 1052, 6438, 68155, 1420, 41730, 116260, 1394, 9566, 42709, 9374, 1046, 1032, 1053, 16178, 1405, 10673, 1278, 116260, 32090, 1046, 1032, 1054, 22141, 1278, 87016, 1119, 108277, 1408, 1278, 1750, 1268, 1621, 116260, 1394, 1032, 1049, 1048, 1317, 1032, 1049, 1052, 7334, 1044, 19826, 32082, 1317, 22980, 66670, 1046, 1032, 1055, 7209, 27855, 9374, 1317, 9566, 1321, 17966, 3866, 1032, 1049, 1048, 1317, 1032, 1049, 1050, 7334, 1046, 1032, 1056, 30592, 1278, 87016, 1119, 108277, 1562, 1278, 34568, 13810, 1059, 9980, 9374, 1317, 4253, 1044, 1321, 8214, 37173, 1278, 126255, 1046, 1032, 1057, 22141, 1278, 87016, 1119, 108277, 1408, 1278, 1750, 1268, 1621, 116260, 1044, 19826, 5785, 1044, 1032, 1053, 1317, 1032, 1049, 1048, 7334, 1046, 1032, 1049, 1048, 4579, 1672, 1454, 1278, 34568, 13810, 1435, 1261, 1317, 13633, 1505, 4258, 1046, 11], "log