{"id": "78", "question": "how to cook brats", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is how to cook brats:\n\nStep 1: Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat.\n\nStep 2: Lightly oil the grate.\n\nStep 3: Combine beer and onions in a large pot, bring to a boil, and submerge the bratwurst. Add red pepper flakes, garlic powder, salt, and pepper.\n\nStep 4: Simmer the bratwurst in the beer mixture for 10 to 14 minutes, turning occasionally to brown evenly.\n\nStep 5: Remove the bratwurst from the beer mixture and grill it on the preheated grill for an additional 5 to 10 minutes, turning occasionally, until browned and cooked through.\n\nStep 6: Serve the bratwurst with the beer mixture as a topping or side dish.\n\nNote: It's important to prick the bratwurst with a fork before cooking to prevent them from exploding while cooking. Also, cooked bratwurst can be stored in the fridge for up to 5 days or frozen for up to 3 months.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, here is how to cook brats: 1 Prick bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding as they cook. 2 Place bratwurst in a large stock pot with onions, butter, and beer. 3 Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes. 4 Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat. 5 Lightly oil the grill grate. 6 Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill for 10 to 14 minutes, turning occasionally to brown evenly. 7 Reduce heat to medium and cook another 10 to 12 minutes. 8 Remove the bratwurst from the beer mixture; reduce heat to low, and continue cooking the onions. 9 Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill, turning once, 5 to 10 minutes. 10 Serve with the beer mixture as a topping or side.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, here is how to cook brats: 1 Prick bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding as they cook. 2 Place bratwurst in a large stock pot with onions, butter, and beer. 3 Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes. 4 Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat. 5 Lightly oil the grill grate. 6 Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill for 10 to 14 minutes, turning occasionally to brown evenly. 7 Reduce heat to medium and cook another 10 to 12 minutes. 8 Remove the bratwurst from the beer mixture; reduce heat to low, and continue cooking the onions. 9 Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill, turning once, 5 to 10 minutes. 10 Serve with the beer mixture as a topping or side.", "time_sec": 15.635, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 35957, 1408, 1278, 4265, 42679, 1044, 3226, 1395, 2606, 1317, 17966, 2795, 2476, 1058, 1032, 1049, 3216, 1985, 87016, 1119, 108277, 1454, 1261, 40191, 1317, 7495, 2424, 1562, 3543, 7967, 1435, 2127, 17966, 1046, 1032, 1050, 22435, 87016, 1119, 108277, 1294, 1261, 4329, 12169, 3418, 1454, 126255, 1044, 34262, 1044, 1321, 34568, 1046, 1032, 1051, 22435, 1278, 3418, 2136, 9566, 9374, 1321, 2500, 2221, 1394, 1032, 1049, 1053, 1317, 1032, 1050, 1048, 7334, 1046, 1032, 1052, 6438, 68155, 1420, 41730, 116260, 1394, 9566, 42709, 9374, 1046, 1032, 1053, 16178, 1405, 10673, 1278, 116260, 32090, 1046, 1032, 1054, 22141, 1278, 87016, 1119, 108277, 1408, 1278, 1750, 1268, 1621, 116260, 1394, 1032, 1049, 1048, 1317, 1032, 1049, 1052, 7334, 1044, 19826, 32082, 1317, 22980, 66670, 1046, 1032, 1055, 7209, 27855, 9374, 1317, 9566, 1321, 17966, 3866, 1032, 1049, 1048, 1317, 1032, 1049, 1050, 7334, 1046, 1032, 1056, 30592, 1278, 87016, 1119, 108277, 1562, 1278, 34568, 13810, 1059, 9980, 9374, 1317, 4253, 1044, 1321, 8214, 37173, 1278, 126255, 1046, 1032, 1057, 22141, 1278, 87016, 1119, 108277, 1408, 1278, 1750, 1268, 1621, 116260, 1044, 19826, 5785, 1044, 1032, 1053, 1317, 1032, 1049, 1048, 7334, 1046, 1032, 1049, 1048, 4579, 1