{"id": "86", "question": "how to prepare blood slide", "gt": "To prepare a blood slide, you will need a clean glass slide and a drop of blood. Place the slide on a flat surface and add a small drop of blood to one end of the slide. Take another clean slide and touch the blood with one end at a 45-degree angle so that the blood runs along the edge of the slide. Push carefully along the length of the first slide to create a thin smear of blood. Make two smears, allow them to air dry, and label them clearly before placing them in slide transport containers.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to prepare a blood slide: First sterilize the needle with a flame. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface and add one small drop of blood to one end. Take another clean slide, hold it at about a 45-degree angle, touch the blood with one end of this slide so the blood runs along the edge of the first slide by capillary action, and push carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood. Make two smears, allow them to air dry, and label clearly. Once dried, place the slides in provided transport containers.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to prepare a blood slide: First sterilize the needle with a flame. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface and add one small drop of blood to one end. Take another clean slide, hold it at about a 45-degree angle, touch the blood with one end of this slide so the blood runs along the edge of the first slide by capillary action, and push carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood. Make two smears, allow them to air dry, and label clearly. Once dried, place the slides in provided transport containers.", "time_sec": 9.774, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "im