{"id": "97", "question": "typical weather in indiana", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the typical weather in Indiana includes long, warm, humid, and wet summers, and chilly and windy winters. The temperature ranges from 22°F to 85°F throughout the year. The passages also mention snowfall and snow accumulation in specific cities, but do not provide a comprehensive overview of the typical weather in Indiana. Therefore, it is not possible to provide a complete answer based solely on the given passages.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, typical weather in Indiana includes long, warm, humid, and wet summers with chilly and windy winters, and partly cloudy conditions year round. Temperatures typically vary from 22°F to 85°F annually, rarely dropping below 3°F or exceeding 92°F. Indianapolis experiences these patterns, with monthly and yearly averages for snow days and inches provided for Fort Wayne, Gary, Michigan City, and South Bend. The wettest year on record in Indianapolis was 1876 with 57.65 inches of rain, while the driest was 1934 with 24.97 inches.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, typical weather in Indiana includes long, warm, humid, and wet summers with chilly and windy winters, and partly cloudy conditions year round. Temperatures typically vary from 22°F to 85°F annually, rarely dropping below 3°F or exceeding 92°F. Indianapolis experiences these patterns, with monthly and yearly averages for snow days and inches provided for Fort Wayne, Gary, Michigan City, and South Bend. The wettest year on record in Indianapolis was 1876 with 57.65 inches of rain, while the driest was 1934 with 24.97 inches.", "time_sec": 11.187, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 35957, 1408, 1278, 42