{"id": "119", "question": "teresa name meaning", "gt": "The name Teresa is of Greek, American, Italian, and Spanish origin. In Greek and American, it means 'Reap; from Therasia.' In Italian, it is interpreted as 'Harvester.' In Spanish, the name is associated with two popular saints, 'Teresa of Avila' and 'Therese of Lisieux.' The name is also thought to originate from the Greek “therizein” meaning “to harvest, harvester” or from the Greek “theros” meaning “summer”.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the name Teresa has multiple meanings depending on the language and cultural context. In Greek, the name Teresa means \"Reap\" or \"Reaper\" from the word \"Therasia.\" In American usage, it retains the Greek meaning of \"Reap\" from \"Therasia.\" In Italian, Teresa means \"Harvester.\" In Spanish, Teresa is associated with the names of two popular saints: \"Teresa of Avila\" and \"Therese of Lisieux.\" Additionally, the name is thought to derive from the Greek \"therizein,\" meaning \"to harvest, harvester,\" or from \"theros,\" meaning \"summer,\" and is linked to the Greek island of Therasia.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the name Teresa has multiple meanings depending on the language and cultural context. In Greek, the name Teresa means \"Reap\" or \"Reaper\" from the word \"Therasia.\" In American usage, it retains the Greek meaning of \"Reap\" from \"Therasia.\" In Italian, Teresa means \"Harvester.\" In Spanish, Teresa is associated with the names of two popular saints: \"Teresa of Avila\" and \"Therese of Lisieux.\" Additionally, the name is thought to derive from the Greek \"therizein,\" meaning \"to harvest, harvester,\" or from \"theros,\" meaning \"summer,\" and is linked to the Greek island of Therasia.", "time_sec": 13.943, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video