{"id": "120", "question": "teresa name meaning", "gt": "The name Teresa is of Greek origin and means \"Reap; from Therasia\" or \"Harvester\". It is also a Spanish and Italian name and is associated with two popular saints, Teresa of Avila and Therese of Lisieux. The name Theresa is a variation of Teresa and also means \"Reaper; from Therasia\". The etymology of the name is uncertain, but it is thought to come from the Greek words \"therizein\" meaning \"to harvest, harvester\" or \"theros\" meaning \"summer\".", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the name Teresa has multiple meanings depending on the language and cultural context. In Greek, the name Teresa means \"Reap\" or \"Reaper\" from the word \"Therasia.\" In American usage, it retains the Greek meaning of \"Reap\" from \"Therasia.\" In Italian, Teresa means \"Harvester.\" In Spanish, Teresa is associated with the names of two popular saints: \"Teresa of Avila\" and \"Therese of Lisieux.\" Additionally, the name is thought to derive from the Greek \"therizein,\" meaning \"to harvest, harvester,\" or from \"theros,\" meaning \"summer,\" and is linked to the Greek island of Therasia.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the name Teresa has multiple meanings depending on the language and cultural context. In Greek, the name Teresa means \"Reap\" or \"Reaper\" from the word \"Therasia.\" In American usage, it retains the Greek meaning of \"Reap\" from \"Therasia.\" In Italian, Teresa means \"Harvester.\" In Spanish, Teresa is associated with the names of two popular saints: \"Teresa of Avila\" and \"Therese of Lisieux.\" Additionally, the name is thought to derive from the Greek \"therizein,\" meaning \"to harvest, harvester,\" or from \"theros,\" meaning \"summer,\" and is linked to the Greek island of Therasia.", "time_sec": 12.227, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-cod