{"id": "126", "question": "building a lean-to shed", "gt": "Building a lean-to shed involves preparing the site, cutting and assembling the skids, flooring, and walls. To prepare the site, a 4\" layer of compacted gravel is recommended. The skids are cut to 70 2/4\" and set and leveled according to the shed building plans. Two 2 x 6 rim joists are cut at 7 3/4\" and six joists at 44 3/4\". The floor is assembled and set on the skids, checked for square, and anchored to the skids with four joist clip angles. The walls are constructed separately and then raised onto the frame. Pressure-treated 4 by 4s are used for the skids, while 2 by 4s are used for the rim joists and flooring. 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood is attached to the frame for the flooring.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, building a lean-to shed involves: 1. Preparing the site with a 4″ layer of compacted gravel and cutting two 4 x 4 skids to 70 2/4″, then setting and leveling them. 2. Cutting two 2 x 6 rim joists to 7 3/4″ and six joists to 44 3/4″, assembling the floor, setting it on the skids, checking for square, and anchoring the frame to the skids with four joist clip angles. 3. Alternatively, cutting two pressure-treated 4 by 4s to 6 feet for skids, positioning the frame on the skids, toenailing floor joists to the skids when square, attaching 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood flooring, and constructing walls separately before raising them onto the frame. 4. The shed dimensions are 6 feet long by 4 feet wide, with the ability to expand in increments of 2 or 4 feet, and floor framing requires cutting two pressure-treated 2 by 4s to 6 feet for rim joists.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, building a lean-to shed involves: 1. Preparing the site with a 4″ layer of compacted gravel and cutting two 4 x 4 skids to 70 2/4″, then setting and leveling them. 2. Cutting two 2 x 6 rim joists to 7 3/4″ and six joists to 44 3/4″, assembling the floor, setting it on the skids, checking for square, and anchoring the frame to the skids with four joist clip angles. 3. Alternatively, cutting two pressure-treated 4 by 4s to 6 feet for skids, positioning the frame on the skids, toenailing floor joists to the skids when square, attaching 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood flooring, and constructing walls separately before raising them onto the frame. 4. The shed dimensions are 6 feet long by 4 feet wide, with the ability to expand in increments of 2 or 4 feet, and floor framing requires cutting two pressure-treated 2 by 4s to 6 feet for rim joists.", "time_sec": 21.41, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 35957, 1408, 1278, 4265, 42679, 1044, 7654, 1261, 16987, 6793, 42878, 19263, 1058, 1032, 1049, 1046, 90327, 1302, 1278, 5586, 1454, 1261, 1032, 1052, 12000, 6240, 1307, 23070, 1286, 59396, 1321, 23589, 2295, 1032, 1052, 2460, 1032, 1052, 3044, 4807, 1317, 1032, 1055, 1048, 1032, 1050, 1047, 1052, 12000, 1044, 2430, 9436, 1321, 3178, 1302, 2424, 1046, 1032, 1050, 1046, 42698, 3333, 2295, 1032, 1050, 2460, 1032, 1054, 17211, 5552, 3742, 1317, 1032, 1055, 1032, 1051, 1047, 1052, 12000, 1321, 5946, 5552, 3742, 1317, 1032, 1052, 1052, 1032, 1051, 1047, 1052, 12000, 1044, 112443, 1278, 11237, 1044, 9436, 1494, 1408, 1278, 3044, 4807, 1044, 24124, 1394, 12333, 1044, 1321, 126838, 1278, 6448, 1317, 1278, 3044, 4807, 1454, 3946, 5552, 1416, 29446, 28472, 1046, 1032, 1051, 1046, 37346, 1044, 23589, 2295, 6909, 30702, 1032, 1052, 1536, 1032, 1052, 1115, 1317, 1032, 1054, 10509, 1394, 3044, 4807, 1044, 36989, 1278, 6448, 1408, 1278, 3044, 4807, 1044, 46819, 42380, 11237, 5552, 3742, 1317, 1278, 3044, 4807, 2200, 12333, 1044, 85639, 1032, 1051, 1047, 1052, 44830, 25121, 15463, 5243, 1291, 2235, 77468, 10288, 