{"id": "130", "question": "difference between vietnam and india", "gt": "The passages suggest that trends in India are more typical than those in Vietnam, particularly in the area of education. Vietnam's education system is described as relatively equitable, where poorer children receive the same treatment as their better-off counterparts. In contrast, India's early focus was on getting children into school, which involved setting up schools, and training teachers. Politically, India supported Vietnam's independence from France and opposed American involvement in the Vietnam War. Both countries have a history of colonialism, with India being a former colony of the United Kingdom and Vietnam of France. Post-colonization, India experienced division and conflict among Hindus, Muslims and Sikhs. Cultural and economic links between India and Vietnam date back to the 2nd century.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the difference between Vietnam and India lies in their education systems and historical contexts. India's early focus was on establishing schools, training teachers, and providing resources to get children into school, while Vietnam's education system is relatively equitable, ensuring poorer children receive the same opportunities as better-off children, making them not less advantaged in the school system. Historically, India supported Vietnam's independence from France, opposed American involvement in the Vietnam War, and supported Vietnam's unification, with strong bilateral relations and cultural links dating back to the 2nd century. In contrast, France and the United Kingdom, who held large colonies, experienced colonial loss around the same time, with the United Kingdom losing India in 1947 and France losing Indochina (modern-day Vietnam) in 1945, leading to conflicts in India after decolonization due to divisions between Hindus, Muslims, and Sikhs.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the difference between Vietnam and India lies in their education systems and historical contexts. India's early focus was on establishing schools, training teachers, and providing resources to get children into school, while Vietnam's education system is relatively equitable, ensuring poorer children receive the same opportunities as better-off children, making them not less advantaged in the school system. Historically, India supported Vietnam's independence from France, opposed American involvement in the Vietnam War, and supported Vietnam's unification, with strong bilateral relations and cultural links dating back to the 2nd century. In contrast, France and the United Kingdom, who held large colonies, experienced colonial loss around the same time, with the United Kingdom losing India in 1947 and France losing Indochina (modern-day Vietnam) in 1945, leading to conflicts in India after decolonization due to divisions between Hindus, Muslims, and Sikhs.", "time_sec": 16.139, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 35957, 1408, 1278, 4265, 42679, 1044, 1278, 6592, 2396, 18915, 1321, 9269, 22524, 1294, 2034, 9313, 6467, 1321, 15979, 35954, 1046, 9269, 1681, 5124, 6468, 1486, 1408, 32637, 13053, 1044, 7716, 20716, 1044, 1321, 11495, 9281, 1317, 2012, 4974, 2203, 5090, 1044, 3016, 18915, 1681, 9313, 2663, 1395, 10513, 3089, 9059, 1044, 40227, 71062, 4974, 10477, 1278, 2879, 20567, 1435, 4942, 12115, 4974, 1044, 6187, 2424, 1605, 4289, 9849, 6152, 1294, 1278, 5090, 2663, 1046, 18307, 2981, 1044, 9269, 10009, 18915, 1681, 25760, 1562, 5498, 1044, 20630, 5150, 20577, 1294, 1278, 18915, 5674, 1044, 1321, 10009, 18915, 1681, 114352, 1044, 1454, 5666, 40458, 5050, 1321, 11459, 14440, 24948, 2595, 1317, 1278, 1032, 1050, 1298, 8042, 1046, 1656, 9033, 1044, 5498, 1321, 1278