{"id": "133", "question": "how to roast individual garlic cloves", "gt": "To roast individual garlic cloves, preheat your oven to 400°F (205°C). Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the garlic bulb, leaving the skins of the cloves intact. Cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of the cloves to expose them. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up, and drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, rubbing it over the cloves. Roast the cloves in the preheated oven for about 45 minutes to an hour, or until they are softened. Store the roasted garlic cloves in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 10 days.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, how to roast individual garlic cloves: The passages describe roasting whole heads of garlic, not individual cloves. Passage 3 states to \"Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic\" and \"cut 1/4 to a 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic\" as part of the method for whole bulbs. Passage 1 notes roasting time depends on clove size (up to 45 minutes or an hour for large cloves) and storage instructions for roasted garlic. However, the passages do not provide specific steps for roasting individual cloves separately from whole heads, as the method described applies to whole garlic bulbs. The text mentions cutting the top of cloves while keeping them attached to the bulb, but does not detail a process for isolating and roasting individual cloves independently.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, how to roast individual garlic cloves: The passages describe roasting whole heads of garlic, not individual cloves. Passage 3 states to \"Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic\" and \"cut 1/4 to a 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic\" as part of the method for whole bulbs. Passage 1 notes roasting time depends on clove size (up to 45 minutes or an hour for large cloves) and storage instructions for roasted garlic. However, the passages do not provide specific steps for roasting individual cloves separately from whole heads, as the method described applies to whole garlic bulbs. The text mentions cutting the top of cloves while keeping them attached to the bulb, but does not detail a process for isolating and roasting individual cloves independently.", "time_sec": 17.326, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 35957, 1408, 1278, 4265, 42679, 1044, 2606, 1317, 1768, 1642, 4597, 86899, 1573, 14869, 1058, 1531, 42679, 12293, 1768, 30887, 6836, 24337, 1307, 86899, 1044, 1605, 4597, 1573, 14869, 1046, 103039, 1032, 1051, 8164, 1317, 1429, 17851, 1299, 1321, 89782, 1278, 4962, 3093, 14129, 14953, 1307, 1278, 6836, 86899, 75690, 1044, 13355, 28890, 1278, 124005, 1307, 1278, 4597, 1573, 14869, 1307, 86899, 1034, 1321, 1429, 8992, 1032, 1049, 1047, 1052, 1317, 1261, 1032, 1049, 1047, 1050, 34158, 1562, 1278, 3977, 1307, 1573, 14869, 1044, 67625, 1278, 4597, 1573, 14869, 1307, 86899, 1034, 1435, 1805, 1307, 1278, 2866, 1394, 6836, 8450, 5136, 1046, 103039, 1032, 1049, 15031, 1768, 30887, 2142, 14620, 1408, 1573, 2235, 3729, 1319, 1982, 1317, 1032, 1052, 1053, 7334, 1505, 1420, 12271, 1394, 4329, 1573, 14869, 1041, 1321, 9287, 15776, 1394, 1768, 65356, 86899, 1046, 3886, 1044, 1278, 42679, 1653, 1605, 5234, 4811, 9578, 1394, 1768, 30887, 4597, 1573, 14869, 25729, 1562, 6836, 24337, 1044, 1435, 1278, 2866, 5055, 28735, 1317, 6836, 86899, 8450, 5136, 1046, 1531, 3403, 49241, 23589, 1278, 3977, 1307, 1573, 14869, 3016, 18528, 2424, 15205, 1317, 1278, 75690, 1044,