{"id": "137", "question": "how to roast individual garlic cloves", "gt": "To roast individual garlic cloves, follow these steps:\n\n1. Preheat your oven to 400°F (205°C).\n2. Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic.\n3. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to a 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic.\n4. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. (A muffin pan works great for this, as it keeps the garlic bulbs from rolling around.)\n5. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.\n6. Roast in the preheated oven for 45 minutes to an hour, or until the cloves are softened.\n7. Store roasted garlic cloves in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 10 days.\n\nYou can also season the garlic cloves to taste with herbs and spices before roasting.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, how to roast individual garlic cloves: The passages describe roasting whole heads of garlic, not individual cloves. Passage 3 states to \"Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic\" and \"cut 1/4 to a 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic\" as part of the method for whole bulbs. Passage 1 notes roasting time depends on clove size (up to 45 minutes or an hour for large cloves) and storage instructions for roasted garlic. However, the passages do not provide specific steps for roasting individual cloves separately from whole heads, as the method described applies to whole garlic bulbs. The text mentions cutting the top of cloves while keeping them attached to the bulb, but does not detail a process for isolating and roasting individual cloves independently.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, how to roast individual garlic cloves: The passages describe roasting whole heads of garlic, not individual cloves. Passage 3 states to \"Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic\" and \"cut 1/4 to a 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic\" as part of the method for whole bulbs. Passage 1 notes roasting time depends on clove size (up to 45 minutes or an hour for large cloves) and storage instructions for roasted garlic. However, the passages do not provide specific steps for roasting individual cloves separately from whole heads, as the method described applies to whole garlic bulbs. The text mentions cutting the top of cloves while keeping them attached to the bulb, but does not detail a process for isolating and roasting individual cloves independently.", "time_sec": 16.468, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 35957, 1408, 1278, 4265, 42679, 1044, 2606, 1317, 1768, 1642, 4597, 86899, 1573, 14869, 1058, 1531, 42679, 12293, 1768, 30887, 6836, 24337, 1307, 86899, 1044, 1605, 4597, 1573, 14869, 1046, 103039, 1032, 1051, 8164, 1317, 1429, 17851, 1299, 1321, 89782, 1278, 4962, 3093, 14129, 14953, 1307, 1278, 6836, 86899, 75690, 1044, 13355, 28890, 1278, 124005, 1307, 1278, 4597, 1573, 14869, 1307, 86899, 1034, 1321, 1429, 8992, 1032, 1049, 1047, 1052, 1317, 1261, 1032, 1049, 1047, 1050, 34158, 1562, 1278, 3977, 1307, 1573, 14869, 1044, 67625, 1278, 4597, 1573, 14869, 1307, 86899, 1034, 1435, 1805, 1307, 1278, 2866, 1394, 6836, 8450, 5136, 1046, 103039, 1032, 1049, 15031, 1768, 30887, 2142, 14620, 1408, 1573, 2235, 3729, 1319, 1982, 1317, 1032, 1052, 1053, 7334, 1505, 1420, 12271, 1394, 4329, 1573, 14869, 1041, 1321, 9287, 15776,