{"id": "158", "question": "how to factory reset a htc one vx", "gt": "To factory reset an HTC One VX, you can follow the steps mentioned in passage 3. Slide the Notifications panel open, tap on Storage, then Factory data reset, and finally tap on Reset phone and Erase everything.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to factory reset a HTC One VX, first switch off the phone by using the Power rocker, then press and hold the Volume Down and Power buttons together for a couple of seconds until the Bootloader Mode appears on the screen, release all keys, choose the Factory Reset option by pressing the Volume Down button to scroll and the Power key to select, then press and hold the Volume Down + Power key for a couple of seconds, and finally confirm the reset by tapping \"Reset phone\" and then \"Erase everything\" after backing up any data and files you want to keep, as instructed in passage 3.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to factory reset a HTC One VX, first switch off the phone by using the Power rocker, then press and hold the Volume Down and Power buttons together for a couple of seconds until the Bootloader Mode appears on the screen, release all keys, choose the Factory Reset option by pressing the Volume Down button to scroll and the Power key to select, then press and hold the Volume Down + Power key for a couple of seconds, and finally confirm the reset by tapping \"Reset phone\" and then \"Erase everything\" after backing up any data and files you want to keep, as instructed in passage 3.", "time_sec": 11.867, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 35957, 1408, 1278, 4265, 42679, 1044, 1317, 21653, 20143, 1261, 10318, 1067, 5661, 1581, 1088, 1044, 2158, 7530, 2490, 1278, 9916, 153