{"id": "159", "question": "how to factory reset a htc one vx", "gt": "To factory reset an HTC One VX, follow these steps:\n\n1. Switch off the device by holding down the Power button for a while.\n2. Press and hold the Volume Down + Power key for a couple of seconds until Bootloader Mode menu appears on the screen.\n3. From the menu, choose \"Factory Data Reset\" by using Volume buttons to scroll and Power key to select.\n4. Confirm the reset by pressing \"Erase Everything\".\n5. Release all keys when the process is complete.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to factory reset a HTC One VX, first switch off the phone by using the Power rocker, then press and hold the Volume Down and Power buttons together for a couple of seconds until the Bootloader Mode appears on the screen, release all keys, choose the Factory Reset option by pressing the Volume Down button to scroll and the Power key to select, then press and hold the Volume Down + Power key for a couple of seconds, and finally confirm the reset by tapping \"Reset phone\" and then \"Erase everything\" after backing up any data and files you want to keep, as instructed in passage 3.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to factory reset a HTC One VX, first switch off the phone by using the Power rocker, then press and hold the Volume Down and Power buttons together for a couple of seconds until the Bootloader Mode appears on the screen, release all keys, choose the Factory Reset option by pressing the Volume Down button to scroll and the Power key to select, then press and hold the Volume Down + Power key for a couple of seconds, and finally confirm the reset by tapping \"Reset phone\" and then \"Erase everything\" after backing up any data and files you want to keep, as instructed in passage 3.", "time_sec": 10.885, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_think