{"id": "173", "question": "how to soften sugar", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here are some ways to soften sugar:\n\n1. To soften brown sugar, place it in a plastic container with a small piece of plastic wrap or foil over the sugar, and cover tightly. Remove the damp paper towel after a couple of days. (Passage 1)\n2. To soften hardened granulated sugar, preheat the oven to a low temperature (150-200°F), remove the sugar from its package, and place it in an ovenproof container. Warm the sugar in the oven for about 15 minutes, then tap it with a spoon. If it starts to fall apart, leave it in the oven for a longer period of time to completely dry out. Always store granulated sugar in an airtight container. (Passage 2)\n3. To keep brown sugar soft, pack it into the smallest container possible to minimize air exposure. (Passage 3)\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages. The passages do not provide information on how to soften other types of sugar, such as confectioner's sugar.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to soften hardened granulated sugar, preheat the oven to the lowest temperature (150-200 degrees), place the sugar in an ovenproof container, and warm it in the oven for approximately 15 minutes. Tap the sugar with a spoon; if it starts to fall apart, turn off the oven and leave the sugar inside for an hour or two to dry completely. For brown sugar, place it in a plastic container with plastic wrap or foil over the sugar, add a damp paper towel or napkin on top, cover tightly, and remove the damp paper towel after a couple of days. The most efficient way to keep brown sugar soft is to store it in an airtight container, limiting air exposure by using the smallest possible container.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to soften hardened granulated sugar, preheat the oven to the lowest temperature (150-200 degrees), place the sugar in an ovenproof container, and warm it in the oven for approximately 15 minutes. Tap the sugar with a spoon; if it starts to fall apart, turn off the oven and leave the sugar inside for an hour or two to dry completely. For brown sugar, place it in a plastic container with plastic wrap or foil over the sugar, add a damp paper towel or napkin on top, cover tightly, and remove the damp paper towel after a couple of days. The most efficient way to keep brown sugar soft is to store it in an airtight container, limiting air exposure by using the smallest possible container.", "time_sec": 14.342, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 35957, 1408, 1278, 4265, 42679, 1044, 1317, 6444, 1262, 100152, 7272, 6557, 24224, 1044, 1750, 68155, 1278, 47139, 1317, 1278, 20755, 6138, 1319, 1049, 1053, 1048, 1045, 1050, 1048, 1048, 17633, 1574, 3535, 1278, 24224, 1294, 1420, 47139, 65708, 11024, 1044, 1321, 15701, 1494, 1294, 1278, 47139, 1394, 11267, 1032, 1049, 1053, 7334, 1046, 58008, 1278, 24224, 1454, 1261, 104626, 1059, 1693, 1494, 16896, 1317, 6962, 13292, 1044, 3884, 2490, 1278, 47139, 1321, 9288, 1278, 24224, 6625, 1394, 1420, 12271, 1505, 2295, 1317, 12689, 10185, 1046, 2898, 22980, 24224, 1044, 3535, 1494, 1294, 1261, 17985, 11024, 1454, 17985, 30711, 1505, 69054, 2136, 1278, 24224, 1044, 2229, 1261, 49922, 7873, 74537, 1505, 11261, 7533, 1408, 3977, 1044, 6432, 40363, 1044, 1321, 8559, 1278, 49922, 7873, 74537, 2453, 1261, 8580, 1307, 5072, 1046, 1531, 2725, 12871, 3039, 1317, 5807, 22980, 24224, 6444, 1395, 1317, 8141, 1494, 1294, 1420, 4864, 1116, 1620, 11024, 1044, 31925, 4864, 11915, 1536, 2505, 1278, 36111, 4171, 11024, 1046, 11], "logp_list": [-0.0, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0004, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0085, -0.9361, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.4517, -0.4929, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.5408, -0.0494, -0.0, -0.4409, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.1324, -0.0