{"id": "180", "question": "psychological effects of hugging", "gt": "Hugging has significant psychological effects. It creates a warm feeling that affects the entire body, akin to the effect of many drugs operating simultaneously. This could be due to the feeling of a loving embrace, leading to good relationships and emotional intimacy. It also enhances empathy and listening skills, which can lead to a psychological hug. Furthermore, research has found that hugging can significantly reduce worries about mortality and boost self-esteem. This soothing effect can be achieved even when hugging an inanimate object like a teddy bear.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, psychological effects of hugging include: it can lead to good relationships, emotional intimacy, and happy marriages through the use of empathy and listening skills (passage 2); it can make a conversation partner feel like they are receiving a hug, described as a psychological hug (passage 2); and it significantly reduces worry of mortality related to existential fears, even when hugging an inanimate object like a teddy bear (passage 3).", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, psychological effects of hugging include: it can lead to good relationships, emotional intimacy, and happy marriages through the use of empathy and listening skills (passage 2); it can make a conversation partner feel like they are receiving a hug, described as a psychological hug (passage 2); and it significantly reduces worry of mortality related to existential fears, even when hugging an inanimate object like a teddy bear (passage 3).", "time_sec": 8.752, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 35957, 1408, 1278, 4265, 42679, 1044, 23690, 5598, 1307, 39638, 7366, 