{"id": "182", "question": "psychological effects of hugging", "gt": "Based on the given passages, we can see that the physiological effects of hugging are numerous and significant. Hugs affect the entire body and can potentially be compared to the effects of multiple drugs operating at once. Furthermore, the act of hugging can also have psychological effects. Empathic listening can lead to emotional intimacy and happy relationships, as well as making conversation partners feel like they are receiving a hug, which can provide comfort and ease their existential fears. Overall, the psychological effects of hugging are positive and suggest that this simple gesture can have a significant impact on our emotional and physical wellbeing.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, psychological effects of hugging include: it can lead to good relationships, emotional intimacy, and happy marriages through the use of empathy and listening skills (passage 2); it can make a conversation partner feel like they are receiving a hug, described as a psychological hug (passage 2); and it significantly reduces worry of mortality related to existential fears, even when hugging an inanimate object like a teddy bear (passage 3).", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, psychological effects of hugging include: it can lead to good relationships, emotional intimacy, and happy marriages through the use of empathy and listening skills (passage 2); it can make a conversation partner feel like they are receiving a hug, described as a psychological hug (passage 2); and it significantly reduces worry of mortality related to existential fears, even when hugging an inanimate object like a teddy bear (passage 3).", "time_sec": 8.74, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "record_pro