{"id": "183", "question": "how to cook a small prime rib roast in oven", "gt": "Before cooking the prime rib roast, let it stand at room temperature for at least 1 hour. Preheat the oven to 375 degrees F. Season the roast with a small amount of salt and lots of fresh ground black pepper. Place the roast on a rack in a pan with the rib side down and the fatty side up. Roast it in the oven for 1 hour. After cooking, you can prepare au jus by placing the roasting pan on the stove over high heat. Add wine and cook for 8-10 minutes, stirring and scraping any brown bits. Add beef stock and cook to reduce the juice by half, which might take about 20 minutes. Add salt and pepper to taste.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to cook a small prime rib roast in oven: 1 Set oven to 450°F and allow the oven to preheat for a minimum of 15 minutes. 2 Season the roast with only a small amount of salt but lots of fresh ground black pepper (using any other spices will take away the flavor from the prime rib!). 3 Place the roast on a rack in the pan with the rib side down and the fatty side up. 4 Rub the roast with House Seasoning. 5 Roast for 1 hour. 6 Turn off the oven. 7 Allow the roast to stand at room temperature for at least 1 hour. 8 While the roast is resting, prepare the au jus by placing the roasting pan on top of the stove over high heat, adding wine, cooking for 8-10 minutes while stirring and scraping brown bits, adding beef stock, cooking and reducing the juice by half (about 20 minutes), and adding salt and pepper to taste.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to cook a small prime rib roast in oven: 1 Set oven to 450°F and allow the oven to preheat for a minimum of 15 minutes. 2 Season the roast with only a small amount of salt but lots of fresh ground black pepper (using any other spices will take away the flavor from the prime rib!). 3 Place the roast on a rack in the pan with the rib side down and the fatty side up. 4 Rub the roast with House Seasoning. 5 Roast for 1 hour. 6 Turn off the oven. 7 Allow the roast to stand at room temperature for at least 1 hour. 8 While the roast is resting, prepare the au jus by placing the roasting pan on top of the stove over high heat, adding wine, cooking for 8-10 minutes while stirring and scraping brown bits, adding beef stock, cooking and reducing the juice by half (about 20 minutes), and adding salt and pepper to taste.", "time_sec": 19.761, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 35957, 1408, 1278, 4265, 42679, 1044, 1317, 17966, 1261, 3709, 8156, 16120, 1768, 1642, 1294, 47139, 1058, 1032, 1049, 7916, 47139, 1317, 1032, 1052, 1053, 1048, 4372, 1070, 1321, 3894, 1278, 47139, 1317, 1750, 68155, 1394, 1261, 11835, 1307, 1032, 1049, 1053, 7334, 1046, 1032, 1050, 27322, 1278, 1768, 1642, 1454, 2342, 1261, 3709, 5647, 1307, 14091, 1809, 26760, 1307, 14420, 7161, 7244, 61170, 1319, 4125, 2258, 2147, 119548, 2084, 4069, 5109, 1278, 52288, 1562, 1278, 8156, 16120, 126385, 1032, 1051, 22435, 1278, 1768, 1642, 1408, 1261, 57164, 1294, 1278, 6114, 1454, 1278, 16120, 4258, 3151, 1321, 1278, 28138, 4258, 2015, 1046, 1032, 1052, 17922, 1278, 1768, 1642, 1454, 8776, 27322, 1302, 1046, 1032, 1053, 3883, 1642, 1394, 1032, 1049, 12271, 1046, 1032, 1054, 14910, 2490, 1278, 47139, 1046, 1032, 1055, 60362, 1278, 1768, 1642, 1317, 3679, 1513, 5349, 6138, 1394, 1513, 4403, 1032, 1049, 12271, 1046, 1032, 1056, 9076, 1278, 1768, 1642, 1395, 38235, 1044, 21907, 1278, 1817, 1475, 1374, 1536, 32283, 1278, 1768, 30887, 6114, 1408, 3977, 1307, 1278, 98018, 2136, 2738, 9374, 1044, 12327, 23592, 1044, 37173, 1394, 1032, 1056, 1045, 1049, 1048, 7334, 3016, 57172, 1321, 124130, 22980, 18490, 1044, 12327, 60948, 12169, 1044, 37173, 1321, 17291, 1278