{"id": "193", "question": "how to attach multiple picture frames together", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here are some steps for attaching multiple picture frames together:\n\nPassage 1: Table-Stand Grouping\nTo join two or three frames together, you can use identical frames or one larger frame as the middle piece. Place the frames beside each other to see if you like the effect, and then mark the hinge placement on the connecting sides. Attach two small hinges to the marked areas to join the frames together.\n\nPassage 2: Hanging Multiple Pictures Together\nBefore attaching the frames together, test different arrangements of the group of multiple pictures on the floor. Once you have decided on the layout, screw the frames to the backer board, repeating the process for each frame. Attach a hanging wire to the back of the frames and hang them on the wall to enjoy the finished result.\n\nPassage 3: Attaching Frames Together\nTo attach two frames together, place them back to back and mark the hinge placement on the connecting sides. The placement should be the same distance from the bottom edge of each frame to ensure stability when the grouped pictures are placed on a table. Attach two small hinges to the marked areas to join the frames together.\n\nIn conclusion, the recommended method for attaching multiple picture frames together involves using identical or matching frames, marking the hinge placement on the connecting sides, and attaching small hinges to join the frames together. It's also important to test different arrangements of the group of pictures on the floor before attaching the frames together, and to ensure that the frames are securely attached to the backer board before hanging them on the wall.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to attach multiple picture frames together: First, select two or three frames of the same wood molding. For joining two together, use identical frames. For joining three together, choose either three of the same or one which is larger to be the middle frame. Lay them beside each other to see if you like the effect. Put two frames together back to back, and mark the hinge placement. The placement must be the same distance from the bottom edges of each frame to ensure that the grouped pictures stand securely on the table top. Attach two small hinges to the connecting sides of the frames.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to attach multiple picture frames together: First, select two or three frames of the same wood molding. For joining two together, use identical frames. For joining three together, choose either three of the same or one which is larger to be the middle frame. Lay them beside each other to see if you like the effect. Put two frames together back to back, and mark the hinge placement. The placement must be the same distance from the bottom edges of each frame to ensure that the grouped pictures stand securely on the table top. Attach two small hinges to the connecting sides of the frames.", "time_sec": 10.369, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 35957, 1408, 1278, 4265, 42679, 1044, 1317, 14722, 6245, 13083, 24751, 5823, 1058, 7610, 1044, 5762, 2295, 1505, 3300, 24751, 1307, 1278, 2879, 12603, 75224, 1046, 2898, 31427, 2295, 5823, 1044, 2210, 18535, 24751, 1046, 2898, 31427, 3300, 5823, 1044, 12729, 5250, 3300, 1307, 1278, 2879, 1505, 1925, 1799, 1395, 9039, 1317, 1402, 1278, 9949, 6448, 1046, 57340, 2424, 25644, 2744, 2147, 1317, 3219, 1693, 1636, 2479, 1278, 2851, 1046, 21374, 2295, 24751, 5823, 2595, 1317, 2595, 1044, 1321, 3780, 1278, 72443, 30880, 1046, 1531, 30880, 4016, 1402, 1278, 2879, 7786, 1562, 1278, 9478, 20978, 1307, 2744, 6448, 1317, 11811, 1455, 1278, 43404, 23874, 3679, 