{"id": "212", "question": "differences between elements compounds and mixtures", "gt": "Here are my answers to the question based on the provided passages:\n\nQ: What are the differences between elements, compounds, and mixtures?\nA: Based on the passages provided, here are the differences between elements, compounds, and mixtures:\n\nElements:\n\n* Are the purest form of a chemical substance (Passage 3)\n* Consist of only one type of atom with the same number of protons (Passage 3)\n\nCompounds:\n\n* Are substances composed of two or more different elements (Passage 3)\n* Are also pure substances (Passage 3)\n\nMixtures:\n\n* Contain two or more substances that are relatively easy to separate (Passage 1)\n* Have a variable composition (Passage 2)\n* Show the properties of their constituent substances (Passage 2)\n* Can be separated by physical means (Passage 2)", "pred": "Based on the given passages, elements are the purest form of a chemical substance composed of only one type of atom with the same number of protons, compounds are pure substances made of two or more different elements chemically bonded together, and mixtures are physical combinations of elements or compounds where the parts are not chemically bonded, retain their own identity, can be separated by physical means, have variable composition, and show the properties of their constituent substances.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, elements are the purest form of a chemical substance composed of only one type of atom with the same number of protons, compounds are pure substances made of two or more different elements chemically bonded together, and mixtures are physical combinations of elements or compounds where the parts are not chemically bonded, retain their own identity, can be separated by physical means, have variable composition, and show the properties of their constituent 