{"id": "223", "question": "how to fix lift valve in toilet", "gt": "Based on the given passages, to fix a lift valve in a toilet, you should follow these steps:\n1. Shut off the water supply valve to the toilet.\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms and remove the broken lift chain.\n3. Install a new flapper valve and chain.\n4. Adjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links.\n5. Cut off any excess lift chain to prevent tangling.\n6. Push the solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle and secure it tightly.\n7. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm closest to the edge.\n8. Use pliers to securely fasten the chain.\n9. Turn the water valve back on.\n10. Test the flush of the toilet and adjust the chain if needed.\n\nNote: The given passages provide step-by-step instructions for fixing a lift valve in a toilet.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to fix the lift valve in a toilet: Step 1: Shut off the water supply valve to the toilet. Step 2: Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms and remove what’s left of the broken lift chain from the lift arm. Step 4: Open the water valve to fill the tank and flush the toilet to check for correct operation. If needed, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links. Cut off the excess lift chain to prevent it from getting tangled. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle; if a screw is included, screw it in tightly until there is no more give and it is secure. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm (the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm) and use pliers to ensure it is securely fastened. Turn the water valve back on and test the flush; if the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to fix the lift valve in a toilet: Step 1: Shut off the water supply valve to the toilet. Step 2: Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms and remove what’s left of the broken lift chain from the lift arm. Step 4: Open the water valve to fill the tank and flush the toilet to check for correct operation. If needed, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links. Cut off the excess lift chain to prevent it from getting tangled. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle; if a screw is included, screw it in tightly until there is no more give and it is secure. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm (the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm) and use pliers to ensure it is securely fastened. Turn the water valve back on and test the flush; if the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.", "time_sec": 17.926, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 35957, 1408, 1278, 4265, 42679, 1044, 1317, 8786, 1278, 17443, 18044, 1294, 1261, 64403, 1058, 25181, 1032, 1049, 1058, 3073, 1341, 2490, 1278, 4180, 11299, 18044, 1317, 1278, 64403, 1046, 25181, 1032, 1050, 1058, 30592, 1278, 3992, 2327, 41972, 18044, 1536, 91065, 1494, 2490, 1278, 34409, 11203, 1321, 8559, 2549, 2190, 3979, 1307, 1278, 17303, 17443, 12099, 1562, 1278, 17443, 5882, 1046, 25181, 1032, 1052, 1058, 9453, 1278, 4180, 18044, 1317, 12369, 1278, 18901, 1321, 49785, 1278, 64403, 1317, 4206, 1394, 6298, 7685, 1046, 3367, 6618, 1044, 3346, 15080, 1278, 17443, 12099, 1536, 11090, 1278, 8893, 29446, 2015, 1505, 3151, 1261, 8580, 1307, 14440, 1046, 42698, 2490, 1278, 15570, 17443, 12099, 1317, 7495, 1494, 1562, 7796, 130659, 1046, 64947, 1278, 3709, 8978, 2362, 1307, 1278, 64403, 17443, 5882,