{"id": "248", "question": "difference between feha and ada", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here's a brief answer to the question:\n\nThe main difference between FEHA and ADA is that FEHA applies to all employers in California, regardless of size or sector, while ADA applies to private employers with 4 to 15 employees and does not cover public employers. Additionally, FEHA has a broader definition of disability, requiring only that a mental or physical disability limit a major life activity, whereas ADA requires a substantial limitation.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the difference between FEHA and ADA is that the ADA applies to all private sector employers with four to fifteen employees and distinguishes between private and public employers, while the FEHA affects more employees and does not distinguish between private and public employers. Additionally, under the ADA, a disability requires a physical or mental impairment that substantially limits a major life activity, whereas the FEHA requires only that a mental and physical disability limit a major life activity, without the requirement of a substantial limitation.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the difference between FEHA and ADA is that the ADA applies to all private sector employers with four to fifteen employees and distinguishes between private and public employers, while the FEHA affects more employees and does not distinguish between private and public employers. Additionally, under the ADA, a disability requires a physical or mental impairment that substantially limits a major life activity, whereas the FEHA requires only that a mental and physical disability limit a major life activity, without the requirement of a substantial limitation.", "time_sec": 11.142, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"vide