{"id": "271", "question": "earliest signs and symptoms of pregnancy", "gt": "The earliest signs of pregnancy often include mood swings and unusual emotional behavior due to a flood of hormones in the body. Dizziness can also occur as pregnancy causes blood vessels to dilate and blood pressure to drop. Other early symptoms can include a missed period, bloating, spotting, and cramping. Approximately half of all pregnant women experience nausea and vomiting, and around 3 in 10 women experience nausea without vomiting, with these symptoms typically starting around six weeks after their last period.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the earliest signs and symptoms of pregnancy include a missed period, bloating, spotting, cramping, mood swings, and dizziness. Passage 2 states that many women know a missed period may indicate pregnancy, but also notes bloating, spotting, and cramping as easily overlooked early signs. Passage 1 describes mood swings resulting from hormonal changes and dizziness caused by blood vessel dilation and dropping blood pressure. Passage 3 mentions nausea and vomiting occurring around six weeks after the last period, which is also an early symptom.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the earliest signs and symptoms of pregnancy include a missed period, bloating, spotting, cramping, mood swings, and dizziness. Passage 2 states that many women know a missed period may indicate pregnancy, but also notes bloating, spotting, and cramping as easily overlooked early signs. Passage 1 describes mood swings resulting from hormonal changes and dizziness caused by blood vessel dilation and dropping blood pressure. Passage 3 mentions nausea and vomiting occurring around six weeks after the last period, which is also an early symptom.", "time_sec": 11.871, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": fa