{"id": "280", "question": "what is severe osteoporosis", "gt": "Based on the given passages, severe osteoporosis refers to a advanced stage of the disease where the bones have weakened significantly, leading to severe bone loss and increased risk of fractures. At this stage, symptoms such as back pain, loss of height, and fractures are more pronounced and frequent. The risk of fractures is particularly high in the spine, hips, and wrists, and can occur even without a fall or injury.\n\nIn summary, severe osteoporosis is characterized by significant bone weakening, heightened risk of fractures, and more pronounced symptoms.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, severe osteoporosis is a condition where bone density loss has progressed to the point that bones become so weak they can compress, leading to symptoms such as back pain, loss of height over time with a stooped posture, and fractures of the vertebrae, wrists, hips, or other bones, often occurring without a fall or injury, particularly in the spine or hips which support the body's weight.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, severe osteoporosis is a condition where bone density loss has progressed to the point that bones become so weak they can compress, leading to symptoms such as back pain, loss of height over time with a stooped posture, and fractures of the vertebrae, wrists, hips, or other bones, often occurring without a fall or injury, particularly in the spine or hips which support the body's weight.", "time_sec": 8.279, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 35957, 1408, 1278, 4265, 42679, 1044, 13015, 95833, 1395, 1261, 6570, 2478, 12442, 10154, 6410, 1934, 67742, 1317, 1278, 2862, 1455, 35246, 6127, 1878, 10824, 2127, 1710, 33469,