{"id": "287", "question": "how to cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven", "gt": "To cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven, preheat the oven to 325 degrees F. Place the frozen roast in a roasting pan and rub the surface with olive oil and season with salt, pepper, and desired seasonings. Place the roast, uncovered, in the preheated oven. Cook for about 20-30 minutes per pound or until the internal temperature reaches 150 degrees F. Once cooked, cover the roast with aluminum foil and let it sit for 30 minutes before serving.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, how to cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven: Preheat the oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit. Place the frozen pork loin in a shallow baking pan on top of a roasting rack with the fat of the pork loin facing upwards. Cook the pork loin for about 20-30 minutes per pound. Insert a meat thermometer and test the meat after cooking. When the internal temperature of the meat reaches 150 degrees Fahrenheit, it is ready to be taken out of the oven. Cover the roast with aluminum foil and let it sit for 30 minutes before serving.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, how to cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven: Preheat the oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit. Place the frozen pork loin in a shallow baking pan on top of a roasting rack with the fat of the pork loin facing upwards. Cook the pork loin for about 20-30 minutes per pound. Insert a meat thermometer and test the meat after cooking. When the internal temperature of the meat reaches 150 degrees Fahrenheit, it is ready to be taken out of the oven. Cover the roast with aluminum foil and let it sit for 30 minutes before serving.", "time_sec": 13.656, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 