{"id": "295", "question": "what is the proper way to fertilize your grass", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the proper way to fertilize your grass is to:\n\n1. Fertilize at the right time of year, which is at the beginning of the growing season, and varies for different types of grasses.\n2. Choose a fertilizer that is suitable for your type of grass and soil pH, as determined by a soil test.\n3. Apply the fertilizer in a perpendicular pattern, avoiding over-fertilization, which can be determined by checking if the leaf blades bounce back up after being stepped on.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the proper way to fertilize your grass is to fertilize at the right time of year, specifically at the beginning of the growing season when the grass begins to turn green for warm season grasses, know your grass type to determine the appropriate fertilizer and frequency, do a pH soil test to determine the correct fertilizer pH, measure your lawn, and apply the fertilizer in a perpendicular pattern while ensuring the lawn is not over-fertilized by checking if the leaf blade bounces back up.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the proper way to fertilize your grass is to fertilize at the right time of year, specifically at the beginning of the growing season when the grass begins to turn green for warm season grasses, know your grass type to determine the appropriate fertilizer and frequency, do a pH soil test to determine the correct fertilizer pH, measure your lawn, and apply the fertilizer in a perpendicular pattern while ensuring the lawn is not over-fertilized by checking if the leaf blade bounces back up.", "time_sec": 11.361, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 35957, 1408, 1278, 4265, 