{"id": "296", "question": "what are examples of potential and kinetic energy?", "gt": "Examples of kinetic energy include an airplane in flight, due to its large mass and fast velocity, and a baseball thrown by a pitcher, which can have a large amount of kinetic energy due to its fast velocity. Examples of potential energy include gravitational potential energy, which is the energy stored in an object as the result of its vertical position or height, and elastic potential energy. Other activities like a car moving, a ball rolling, a river flowing, an athlete running, rides in an amusement park, and a satellite in orbit also involve potential and kinetic energy.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, examples of potential energy include a car at a certain height (implied by gravitational potential energy discussion), a ball at a certain height, a river at a certain elevation, a satellite in orbit, and an object in a position to fall due to gravity. Examples of kinetic energy include an airplane in flight, a baseball thrown by a pitcher, a car moving, a ball rolling, a river flowing, an athlete running, rides in an amusement park, and a satellite in orbit.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, examples of potential energy include a car at a certain height (implied by gravitational potential energy discussion), a ball at a certain height, a river at a certain elevation, a satellite in orbit, and an object in a position to fall due to gravity. Examples of kinetic energy include an airplane in flight, a baseball thrown by a pitcher, a car moving, a ball rolling, a river flowing, an athlete running, rides in an amusement park, and a satellite in orbit.", "time_sec": 9.672, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "record_process": true, "token_ids":