{"id": "297", "question": "what are examples of potential and kinetic energy?", "gt": "Based on the given passages, examples of potential energy include an object's gravitational potential energy due to its vertical position or height, and elastic potential energy stored in objects due to their deformation. Examples of kinetic energy include an airplane's kinetic energy in flight due to its large mass and fast velocity, a baseball's kinetic energy due to its fast velocity despite its small mass, and the kinetic energy possessed by objects in motion such as cars, balls, rivers, athletes, amusement park rides, and satellites in orbit.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, examples of potential energy include a car at a certain height (implied by gravitational potential energy discussion), a ball at a certain height, a river at a certain elevation, a satellite in orbit, and an object in a position to fall due to gravity. Examples of kinetic energy include an airplane in flight, a baseball thrown by a pitcher, a car moving, a ball rolling, a river flowing, an athlete running, rides in an amusement park, and a satellite in orbit.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, examples of potential energy include a car at a certain height (implied by gravitational potential energy discussion), a ball at a certain height, a river at a certain elevation, a satellite in orbit, and an object in a position to fall due to gravity. Examples of kinetic energy include an airplane in flight, a baseball thrown by a pitcher, a car moving, a ball rolling, a river flowing, an athlete running, rides in an amusement park, and a satellite in orbit.", "time_sec": 10.32, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 35957, 1408, 1278, 42