{"id": "299", "question": "how to make hot water heater circulate", "gt": "To make a hot water heater circulate, a hot water circulation pump can be installed. This pump sends cool water from the pipes back to the water heater through a return line, while simultaneously pulling hot water from the heater to keep it hot. This continuous loop ensures that hot water is always available.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to make a hot water heater circulate, a hot water circulation pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line, and the pump circulates this water through the water heater as needed to keep it hot, creating a continuous loop of water through the water heater. Alternatively, recirculating pumps rapidly pull hot water from a water heater while simultaneously sending cool water from the hot water lines back to the water heater to be reheated and reused, with demand systems being controlled by a button, timer, or motion sensor.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to make a hot water heater circulate, a hot water circulation pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line, and the pump circulates this water through the water heater as needed to keep it hot, creating a continuous loop of water through the water heater. Alternatively, recirculating pumps rapidly pull hot water from a water heater while simultaneously sending cool water from the hot water lines back to the water heater to be reheated and reused, with demand systems being controlled by a button, timer, or motion sensor.", "time_sec": 10.733, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 35957, 1408, 1278, 4265, 42679, 1044, 1317, 3180, 1261, 8480, 4180, 69033, 40