{"id": "332", "question": "how to get rid of ticks from dogs", "gt": "To get rid of ticks from dogs, first, check common tick hiding places such as inside and behind the dog's ears and around the eyes. Once you locate a tick, use a pair of tweezers to grasp the tick's head where it attaches to the skin. If you plan to use your fingers, wear gloves. Pull on the tick gently and steadily to avoid leaving part of the tick's mouth behind, which can cause an infection. Regular use of tick control products can also prevent ticks from attaching to your dog. Your veterinarian can advise you about the best product for your dog and your situation. Flea and tick shampoos can kill the ticks that are already on your pet.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, how to get rid of ticks from dogs: Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin, wear gloves if using fingers, and pull the tick gently and steadily to avoid leaving the mouth behind which can cause infection, and check inside and behind the dog's ears and around the eyes as favorite tick hiding places.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, how to get rid of ticks from dogs: Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin, wear gloves if using fingers, and pull the tick gently and steadily to avoid leaving the mouth behind which can cause infection, and check inside and behind the dog's ears and around the eyes as favorite tick hiding places.", "time_sec": 7.711, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 35957, 1408, 1278, 4265, 42679, 1044, 2606, 1317, 2012, 15515, 1307, 76849, 1562, 25007, 1058, 13516, 1261, 10217, 1307, 13791, 8019, 1428, 1317, 51776, 1278, 3518, 1307, 1278, 41596, 247