{"id": "335", "question": "how to get rid of ticks from dogs", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here's how to get rid of ticks from dogs:\n\n1. Check inside and behind the dog's ears and around its eyes, which are common hiding places for ticks. (Passage 1)\n2. Use tick control products recommended by a veterinarian to prevent ticks from attaching to the dog. (Passage 2)\n3. Remove ticks from the dog using a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin. (Passage 1)\n\nUnable to answer based on the given passages whether there are any specific products or methods for getting rid of ticks from dogs that are already infested.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, how to get rid of ticks from dogs: Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin, wear gloves if using fingers, and pull the tick gently and steadily to avoid leaving the mouth behind which can cause infection, and check inside and behind the dog's ears and around the eyes as favorite tick hiding places.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, how to get rid of ticks from dogs: Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin, wear gloves if using fingers, and pull the tick gently and steadily to avoid leaving the mouth behind which can cause infection, and check inside and behind the dog's ears and around the eyes as favorite tick hiding places.", "time_sec": 7.967, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 35957, 1408, 1278, 4265, 42679, 1044, 2606, 1317, 2012, 15515, 1307, 76849, 1562, 25007, 1058, 13516, 1261, 10217, 1307, 13791, 8019, 1428, 1317, 51776, 1278, 3518, 1307, 1278, 41596, 2478, 1494, 14722, 1264, 1317, 1278, 9877, 1044, 18