{"id": "380", "question": "what is dmso used for", "gt": "Based on the given passages, DMSO is used for various purposes, including:\n\n1. Industrial uses: As an antifreeze and solvent for a wide range of chemicals.\n2. Medical uses: To relieve pain, reduce swelling and inflammation, promote healing, and treat a variety of medical ailments such as burns, scleroderma, and soft tissue damage.\n3. Pain relief: For muscles and joints, and as a general pain reliever applied to the skin.\n4. Skin care: To penetrate skin and tissue and enter the bloodstream.\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question \"What is DMSO used for?\" can be summarized as: DMSO is used for various industrial, medical, and personal care purposes, including pain relief, wound healing, and skin care.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, DMSO is used as an antifreeze, a solvent for a wide range of chemicals, and in industrial processes like converting trees to paper. Medically, it is used to relieve pain, reduce swelling and inflammation, treat burns, scleroderma, soft tissue damage, local tissue death, skin ulcers, and minor cuts and burns, with studies showing it promotes healing and speeds recovery.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, DMSO is used as an antifreeze, a solvent for a wide range of chemicals, and in industrial processes like converting trees to paper. Medically, it is used to relieve pain, reduce swelling and inflammation, treat burns, scleroderma, soft tissue damage, local tissue death, skin ulcers, and minor cuts and burns, with studies showing it promotes healing and speeds recovery.", "time_sec": 6.796, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 35957, 1408, 1278, 4265, 42679, 1044, 66300, 1395, 2434, 1435, 1420, 65