{"id": "381", "question": "how to arrange an excel sheet alphabetical", "gt": "To arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, first click on the Select All button at the intersection of your row and column headings. Then, switch to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon and locate the Sort & Filter group. Click on the Sort option. Click on the Sort By drop-down menu to select a column by name. The names correspond to the headings typed in the first row of your data. Alternatively, you can use Kutools for Excel's Sort Sheets tool to sort all worksheets.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically: 1. Click on the Select All button at the intersection of row and column headings to select all cells. 2. Switch to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon and locate the Sort & Filter group. 3. Click on the Sort option. 4. Click on the Sort By drop-down menu to select a column by name, such as the Product column (column B). 5. Select alphabetical order (A to Z) from the options. 6. Click OK to apply the sort.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically: 1. Click on the Select All button at the intersection of row and column headings to select all cells. 2. Switch to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon and locate the Sort & Filter group. 3. Click on the Sort option. 4. Click on the Sort By drop-down menu to select a column by name, such as the Product column (column B). 5. Select alphabetical order (A to Z) from the options. 6. Click OK to apply the sort.", "time_sec": 9.284, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 35957, 1408, 1278, 4265, 42679, 1044, 1317, 55428, 1420, 35367, 15241, 46198, 2981, 1058, 1032, 1049, 1046, 30476, 1