{"id": "383", "question": "how to arrange an excel sheet alphabetical", "gt": "To arrange an excel sheet alphabetical, one can follow these steps:\n\n1. Select the Data tab from the toolbar at the top of the screen.\n2. Click on the Sort button and select Custom Sort from the popup menu.\n3. When the Sort window appears, select the data that you wish to sort by. In this example, we want to sort by the Product column (column B) in alphabetical order (A to Z).\n4. Click on the OK button.\n5. The data should now be sorted in alphabetical order.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically: 1. Click on the Select All button at the intersection of row and column headings to select all cells. 2. Switch to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon and locate the Sort & Filter group. 3. Click on the Sort option. 4. Click on the Sort By drop-down menu to select a column by name, such as the Product column (column B). 5. Select alphabetical order (A to Z) from the options. 6. Click OK to apply the sort.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically: 1. Click on the Select All button at the intersection of row and column headings to select all cells. 2. Switch to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon and locate the Sort & Filter group. 3. Click on the Sort option. 4. Click on the Sort By drop-down menu to select a column by name, such as the Product column (column B). 5. Select alphabetical order (A to Z) from the options. 6. Click OK to apply the sort.", "time_sec": 9.367, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 35957, 1408, 1278, 4265, 42679, 1044, 1317, 55428, 1420, 35367, 15241, 46198, 2981, 1058, 1032, 1049, 1046, 30476, 1408, 1278,