{"id": "404", "question": "2006 chevy remove door panel", "gt": "The passage provides step-by-step instructions for removing the rear door panel on a 2006 Chevy HHR. To perform this task, the passenger must locate and remove the two screws inside the door pull cup and the middle of the inside door handle. A pin on the outside edge of the door must also be removed using a door panel removal tool. Once all these steps are completed, the door panel can be carefully pulled away from the frame, taking care not to damage any wiring connections.\n\nAccordingly, the answer to the question is:\n\nRemoving the rear door panel on a 2006 Chevy HHR involves locating and removing the screws inside the door pull cup and the middle of the inside door handle, as well as removing the pin on the outside edge of the door using a door panel removal tool.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, 2006 Chevy remove door panel: To remove the rear door panel in your Chevy HHR, you will need to remove the two screws located inside of the door pull cup, and there's also one in the middle of the inside door handle. On the outer edge of the door there's also a pin that holds the panel in place, you will need to remove that. Then use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off of the HHR rear door.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, 2006 Chevy remove door panel: To remove the rear door panel in your Chevy HHR, you will need to remove the two screws located inside of the door pull cup, and there's also one in the middle of the inside door handle. On the outer edge of the door there's also a pin that holds the panel in place, you will need to remove that. Then use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off of the HHR rear door.", "time_sec": 8.492, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "a