{"id": "405", "question": "2006 chevy remove door panel", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is the answer to the question:\n\nTo remove the rear door panel in a 2006 Chevy HHR, you should follow these steps:\n\n1. Remove the two screws located inside the door pull cup.\n2. Remove the screw located in the middle of the inside door handle.\n3. Remove the pin on the outer edge of the door that holds the panel in place.\n4. Use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off of the HHR rear door.\n\nIt is important to note that an instructional video is also available that shows the entire process and location of the screws and pin.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, 2006 Chevy remove door panel: To remove the rear door panel in your Chevy HHR, you will need to remove the two screws located inside of the door pull cup, and there's also one in the middle of the inside door handle. On the outer edge of the door there's also a pin that holds the panel in place, you will need to remove that. Then use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off of the HHR rear door.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, 2006 Chevy remove door panel: To remove the rear door panel in your Chevy HHR, you will need to remove the two screws located inside of the door pull cup, and there's also one in the middle of the inside door handle. On the outer edge of the door there's also a pin that holds the panel in place, you will need to remove that. Then use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off of the HHR rear door.", "time_sec": 8.659, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 35957, 1408, 1278, 4265, 42679, 1044, 1032, 1050, 1048, 1048, 1054, 10691, 18952, 8559, 5433, 12321, 1058, 3870, 8559, 127