{"id": "406", "question": "2006 chevy remove door panel", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is the answer to the question:\n\nTo remove the door panel on a 2006 Chevy, you will need to:\n\n1. Remove the two screws located inside the door pull cup.\n2. Remove the screw in the middle of the inside door handle.\n3. Remove the pin that holds the panel in place on the outer edge of the door.\n4. Use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off the rear door.\n5. Remove any wiring connections.\n6. Gently pull the panel away from the frame.\n\nAfter removing the screws and clips, you will be able to remove the door panel. It is recommended to watch an instructional video to see the process and locate the parts mentioned.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, 2006 Chevy remove door panel: To remove the rear door panel in your Chevy HHR, you will need to remove the two screws located inside of the door pull cup, and there's also one in the middle of the inside door handle. On the outer edge of the door there's also a pin that holds the panel in place, you will need to remove that. Then use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off of the HHR rear door.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, 2006 Chevy remove door panel: To remove the rear door panel in your Chevy HHR, you will need to remove the two screws located inside of the door pull cup, and there's also one in the middle of the inside door handle. On the outer edge of the door there's also a pin that holds the panel in place, you will need to remove that. Then use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off of the HHR rear door.", "time_sec": 8.456, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 35957, 1408, 1278, 4265, 42679, 