{"id": "408", "question": "how to make panko crumbs", "gt": "To make panko crumbs, preheat the oven to 300 degrees F (150 degrees C). Push torn pieces or chunks of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs. Spread the crumbs on a baking sheet and bake at 300 degrees F for 6 to 8 minutes, shaking the sheet twice during baking. Remove from the oven and cool completely.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to make panko crumbs: 1) Preheat an oven to 300 degrees F (150 degrees C). 2) Push torn or chunk pieces of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs. 3) Spread the crumbs on a baking sheet. 4) Bake in the preheated oven until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, for 6 to 8 minutes. 5) Shake the sheet twice during baking to evenly dry the crumbs. 6) Remove from the oven and cool completely. Alternatively, 1) Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F. 2) Place bread chunks into a blender carafe, cover and pulse for about 2 minutes until coarse crumbs form. 3) Spread the crumbs evenly on two half sheet pans. 4) Bake until the crumbs just begin to brown and are crisp, about 5 minutes. 5) Cool the crumbs on the pans for 15 to 20 minutes. 6) Transfer to an airtight container and store at room temperature for up to 2 weeks. Be careful not to let the crumbs brown.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to make panko crumbs: 1) Preheat an oven to 300 degrees F (150 degrees C). 2) Push torn or chunk pieces of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs. 3) Spread the crumbs on a baking sheet. 4) Bake in the preheated oven until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, for 6 to 8 minutes. 5) Shake the sheet twice during baking to evenly dry the crumbs. 6) Remove from the oven and cool completely. Alternatively, 1) Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F. 2) Place bread chunks into a blender carafe, cover and pulse for about 2 minutes until coarse crumbs form. 3) Spread the crumbs evenly on two half sheet pans. 4) Bake until the crumbs just begin to brown and are crisp, about 5 minutes. 5) Cool the crumbs on the pans for 15 to 20 minutes. 6) Transfer to an airtight container and store at room temperature for up to 2 weeks. Be careful not to let the crumbs brown.", "time_sec": 19.481, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 35957, 1408, 1278, 4265, 42679, 1044, 1317, 3180, 1274, 2395, 1111, 2989, 67932, 1058, 1032, 1049, 1041, 6438, 68155, 1420, 47139, 1317, 1032, 1051, 1048, 1048, 17633, 1439, 1319, 1049, 1053, 1048, 17633, 1359, 1577, 1032, 1050, 1041, 64947, 12389, 1505, 36561, 17352, 1307, 7496, 27890, 2645, 1278, 114586, 26080, 15739, 1307, 1261, 6939, 18876, 1317, 3180, 61060, 2989, 67932, 1046, 1032, 1051, 1041, 104533, 1278, 2989, 67932, 1408, 1261, 75252, 15241, 1046, 1032, 1052, 1041, 1398, 2082, 1294, 1278, 1750, 1268, 1621, 47139, 4570, 1278, 2989, 67932, 1584, 12689, 1809, 1605, 41847, 1286, 1044, 1394, 1032, 1054, 1317, 1032, 1056, 7334, 1046, 1032, 1053, 1041, 3073, 2082, 1278, 15241, 15449, 3184, 75252, 1317, 66670, 12689, 1278, 2989, 67932, 1046, 1032, 1054, 1041, 30592, 1562, 1278, 47139, 1321, 12921, 10185, 1046, 37346, 1044, 1032, 1049, 1041, 6438, 68155, 1278, 47139, 1317, 1032, 1051, 1048, 1048, 17633, 1439, 1046, 1032, 1050, 1041, 22435, 27890, 63308, 2203, 1261, 2326, 3206, 2382, 21518, 1044, 6432, 1321, 19893, 1394, 2314, 1032, 1050, 7334, 4570, 61060, 2989, 67932, 2071, 1046, 1032, 1051, 1041, 104533, 1278, 2989, 67932, 66670, 1408, 2295, 6420, 15241, 76913, 1046, 1032, 1052, 1041, 1398, 2082, 4570, 1278, 2989, 67932, 2586, 6396, 1317, 22980, 1321, 1584, 72054, 1044, 2314, 1032, 1053, 7334, 1046, 1032, 1053, 1041, 53090, 1278, 2989, 67932, 1408, 1278, 76