{"id": "409", "question": "how to make panko crumbs", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is how to make panko crumbs:\n\nPassage 1 states to push torn pieces of bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs. Then, spread the crumbs on a baking sheet and bake in a preheated oven until they are dry but not toasted, about 6 to 8 minutes.\n\nPassage 2 provides similar instructions, stating to push chunks of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs. Then, spread the crumbs on a baking sheet and bake at 300°F until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, about 6 to 8 minutes.\n\nPassage 3 provides additional information, suggesting to preheat the oven to 300°F before making the crumbs. The passage also recommends using a blender carafe to pulse the bread until coarse crumbs form, and then spreading the crumbs evenly on two half-sheet pans and baking until they just begin to brown and are crisp, about 5 minutes. After cooling the crumbs on the pans for 15 to 20 minutes, transfer them to an airtight container and store them at room temperature for up to 2 weeks.\n\nTherefore, to make panko crumbs based on the provided passages, you can use a food processor or blender to shred or pulse bread into coarse crumbs, and then bake them in a preheated oven until they are dry but not toasted.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to make panko crumbs: 1) Preheat an oven to 300 degrees F (150 degrees C). 2) Push torn or chunk pieces of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs. 3) Spread the crumbs on a baking sheet. 4) Bake in the preheated oven until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, for 6 to 8 minutes. 5) Shake the sheet twice during baking to evenly dry the crumbs. 6) Remove from the oven and cool completely. Alternatively, 1) Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F. 2) Place bread chunks into a blender carafe, cover and pulse for about 2 minutes until coarse crumbs form. 3) Spread the crumbs evenly on two half sheet pans. 4) Bake until the crumbs just begin to brown and are crisp, about 5 minutes. 5) Cool the crumbs on the pans for 15 to 20 minutes. 6) Transfer to an airtight container and store at room temperature for up to 2 weeks. Be careful not to let the crumbs brown.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to make panko crumbs: 1) Preheat an oven to 300 degrees F (150 degrees C). 2) Push torn or chunk pieces of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs. 3) Spread the crumbs on a baking sheet. 4) Bake in the preheated oven until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, for 6 to 8 minutes. 5) Shake the sheet twice during baking to evenly dry the crumbs. 6) Remove from the oven and cool completely. Alternatively, 1) Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F. 2) Place bread chunks into a blender carafe, cover and pulse for about 2 minutes until coarse crumbs form. 3) Spread the crumbs evenly on two half sheet pans. 4) Bake until the crumbs just begin to brown and are crisp, about 5 minutes. 5) Cool the crumbs on the pans for 15 to 20 minutes. 6) Transfer to an airtight container and store at room temperature for up to 2 weeks. Be careful not to let the crumbs brown.", "time_sec": 19.481, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 35957, 1408, 1278, 4265, 42679, 1044, 1317, 3180, 1274, 2395, 1111, 2989, 67932, 1058, 1032, 1049, 1041, 6438, 68155, 1420, 47139, 1317, 1032, 1051, 1048, 1048, 17633, 1439, 1319, 1049, 1053, 1048, 17633, 1359, 1577, 1032, 1050, 1041, 64947, 12389, 1505, 36561, 17352, 1307, 7496, 27890, 2645, 1278, 114586, 26080, 15739, 1307, 1261, 6939, 18876, 1317, 3180, 61060, 2989, 67932, 1046, 1032, 1051, 1041, 104533, 1278, 298