{"id": "410", "question": "how to make panko crumbs", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is how to make panko crumbs:\n\n1. Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F (150 degrees C).\n2. Torn pieces of bread are pushed through the shredding disk of a food processor to create coarse crumbs.\n3. The crumbs are spread on a baking sheet.\n4. The sheet is baked in the preheated oven until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, for 6 to 8 minutes.\n5. The sheet is shaken twice during baking to ensure even drying.\n6. After baking, the crumbs are removed from the oven and allowed to cool completely.\n\nAlternatively, according to passage 2, you can also make panko crumbs by:\n\n1. Pushing chunks of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to create coarse crumbs.\n2. Spreading the crumbs on a baking sheet and baking at 300 degrees F until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, for 6 to 8 minutes.\n3. Shaking the sheet twice during baking.\n4. Being careful not to let the crumbs brown.\n\nFinally, passage 3 provides a third method for making panko crumbs, which involves blending the ingredients in a blender carafe and baking them on half sheet pans until they are crisp and lightly browned.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to make panko crumbs: 1) Preheat an oven to 300 degrees F (150 degrees C). 2) Push torn or chunk pieces of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs. 3) Spread the crumbs on a baking sheet. 4) Bake in the preheated oven until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, for 6 to 8 minutes. 5) Shake the sheet twice during baking to evenly dry the crumbs. 6) Remove from the oven and cool completely. Alternatively, 1) Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F. 2) Place bread chunks into a blender carafe, cover and pulse for about 2 minutes until coarse crumbs form. 3) Spread the crumbs evenly on two half sheet pans. 4) Bake until the crumbs just begin to brown and are crisp, about 5 minutes. 5) Cool the crumbs on the pans for 15 to 20 minutes. 6) Transfer to an airtight container and store at room temperature for up to 2 weeks. Be careful not to let the crumbs brown.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to make panko crumbs: 1) Preheat an oven to 300 degrees F (150 degrees C). 2) Push torn or chunk pieces of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs. 3) Spread the crumbs on a baking sheet. 4) Bake in the preheated oven until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, for 6 to 8 minutes. 5) Shake the sheet twice during baking to evenly dry the crumbs. 6) Remove from the oven and cool completely. Alternatively, 1) Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F. 2) Place bread chunks into a blender carafe, cover and pulse for about 2 minutes until coarse crumbs form. 3) Spread the crumbs evenly on two half sheet pans. 4) Bake until the crumbs just begin to brown and are crisp, about 5 minutes. 5) Cool the crumbs on the pans for 15 to 20 minutes. 6) Transfer to an airtight container and store at room temperature for up to 2 weeks. Be careful not to let the crumbs brown.", "time_sec": 19.544, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 35957, 1408, 1278, 4265, 42679, 1044, 1317, 3180, 1274, 2395, 1111, 2989, 67932, 1058, 1032, 1049, 1041, 6438, 68155, 1420, 47139, 1317, 1032, 1051, 1048, 1048, 17633, 1439, 1319, 1049, 1053, 1048, 17633, 1359, 1577, 1032, 1050, 1041, 64947, 12389, 1505, 36561, 17352, 1307, 7496, 27890, 2645, 1278, 114586, 26080, 15739, 1307, 1261, 6939, 18876, 1317, 3180, 61060, 2989, 67932, 1046, 1032, 1051, 1041, 104533, 1278, 2989, 67932, 1408, 1261, 75252, 15241, 1046, 1032, 1052, 1041, 1398, 2082, 1294, 1278, 1750, 1268, 1621, 47139, 4570, 1278, 2989, 67932, 1584, 12689, 1809, 1605