{"id": "411", "question": "how to make panko crumbs", "gt": "Sure, I can help you with that! Based on the given passages, here's a step-by-step guide on how to make panko crumbs:\n\n1. Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F (150 degrees C).\n2. Push torn pieces of bread or chunks of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs.\n3. Spread the crumbs on a baking sheet.\n4. Bake in preheated oven until crumbs are dry but not toasted, 6 to 8 minutes. Shake the sheet twice during baking to evenly dry the crumbs.\n5. Remove from the oven and cool completely.\n\nIf you want to store the panko crumbs for later use, you can transfer them to an airtight container and keep them at room temperature for up to 2 weeks.\n\nI hope this helps! Let me know if you have any further questions.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to make panko crumbs: 1) Preheat an oven to 300 degrees F (150 degrees C). 2) Push torn or chunk pieces of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs. 3) Spread the crumbs on a baking sheet. 4) Bake in the preheated oven until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, for 6 to 8 minutes. 5) Shake the sheet twice during baking to evenly dry the crumbs. 6) Remove from the oven and cool completely. Alternatively, 1) Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F. 2) Place bread chunks into a blender carafe, cover and pulse for about 2 minutes until coarse crumbs form. 3) Spread the crumbs evenly on two half sheet pans. 4) Bake until the crumbs just begin to brown and are crisp, about 5 minutes. 5) Cool the crumbs on the pans for 15 to 20 minutes. 6) Transfer to an airtight container and store at room temperature for up to 2 weeks. Be careful not to let the crumbs brown.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to make panko crumbs: 1) Preheat an oven to 300 degrees F (150 degrees C). 2) Push torn or chunk pieces of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs. 3) Spread the crumbs on a baking sheet. 4) Bake in the preheated oven until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, for 6 to 8 minutes. 5) Shake the sheet twice during baking to evenly dry the crumbs. 6) Remove from the oven and cool completely. Alternatively, 1) Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F. 2) Place bread chunks into a blender carafe, cover and pulse for about 2 minutes until coarse crumbs form. 3) Spread the crumbs evenly on two half sheet pans. 4) Bake until the crumbs just begin to brown and are crisp, about 5 minutes. 5) Cool the crumbs on the pans for 15 to 20 minutes. 6) Transfer to an airtight container and store at room temperature for up to 2 weeks. Be careful not to let the crumbs brown.", "time_sec": 19.381, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 35957, 1408, 1278, 4265, 42679, 1044, 1317, 3180, 1274, 2395, 1111, 2989, 67932, 1058, 1032, 1049, 1041, 6438, 68155, 1420, 47139, 1317, 1032, 1051, 1048, 1048, 17633, 1439, 1319, 1049, 1053, 1048, 17633, 1359, 1577, 1032, 1050, 1041, 64947, 12389, 1505, 36561, 17352, 1307, 7496, 27890, 2645, 1278, 114586, 26080, 15739, 1307, 1261, 6939, 18876, 1317, 3180, 61060, 2989, 67932, 1046, 1032, 1051, 1041, 104533, 1278, 2989, 67932, 1408, 1261, 75252, 15241, 1046, 1032, 1052, 1041, 1398, 2082, 1294, 1278, 1750, 1268, 1621, 47139, 4570, 1278, 2989, 67932, 1584, 12689, 1809, 1605, 41847, 1286, 1044, 1394, 1032, 1054, 1317, 1032, 1056, 7334, 1046, 1032, 1053, 1041, 3073, 2082, 1278, 15241, 15449, 3184, 75252, 1317, 66670, 12689, 1278, 2989, 67932, 1046, 1032, 1054, 1041, 30592, 1562, 1278, 47139, 1321, 12921, 10185, 1046, 37346, 1044, 1032, 1049, 1041, 6438, 68155, 1278, 47139, 1317, 1032, 1051, 1048, 1048, 17633, 1439, 1046, 1032, 1050, 1041, 22435, 27890, 63308, 2203, 