{"id": "422", "question": "what is a upc description", "gt": "A UPC description refers to the Universal Product Code, a barcode symbology used extensively in multiple countries including the United States, Canada, United Kingdom, Australia, New Zealand, and in Europe. It is used for tracking trade items in stores. UPC consists of 12 numeric digits that are uniquely assigned to each trade item. It is primarily used for scanning of trade items at the point of sale, as per GS1 specifications.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, a UPC (Universal Product Code) is a barcode symbology that consists of 12 numeric digits uniquely assigned to each trade item, widely used in the United States, Canada, United Kingdom, Australia, New Zealand, Europe and other countries for tracking trade items in stores and scanning at point of sale per GS1 specifications.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, a UPC (Universal Product Code) is a barcode symbology that consists of 12 numeric digits uniquely assigned to each trade item, widely used in the United States, Canada, United Kingdom, Australia, New Zealand, Europe and other countries for tracking trade items in stores and scanning at point of sale per GS1 specifications.", "time_sec": 6.09, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 35957, 1408, 1278, 4265, 42679, 1044, 1261, 1608, 9793, 1319, 91090, 14012, 13968, 1041, 1395, 1261, 104431, 120060, 3678, 1455, 15730, 1307, 1032, 1049, 1050, 47845, 35515, 62740, 14451, 1317, 2744, 12191, 5610, 1044, 14769, 2434, 1294, 1278, 4857, 6086, 1044, 9591, 1044, 4857, 15703, 1044, 10243, 1044, 3140, 17492, 1044, 5550, 1321, 2147, 8641, 1394, 26112, 12191, 7748, 1294, 21888, 1321, 27867, 1513, 2862, 1307, 15797, 1651, 39287, 1049, 5