{"id": "449", "question": "how do i file a lien on a semi", "gt": "Unable to answer based on given passages. The passages provided do not contain information on how to file a lien on a semi. Passage 1 discusses the possibility of a creditor placing a lien on a home that has been transferred to a spouse, while passage 2 explains the general process for placing a lien on business property but does not mention semis specifically. Passage 3 describes the documentation and distribution of copies of a lien entry form, but does not provide instructions on how to file a lien. Therefore, without additional information, it is impossible to provide an answer to the question.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to file a lien on a semi, you must first obtain a court order (judgment) directing the debtor to pay what is owed, then file a claim with the court and submit proof of the amounts owed, after which the business must answer and explain why the debt is not owed, and after processing, one copy will be attached to the titling documentation with a copy of the lien fee receipt, one copy with the lien fee receipt will be sent to OTC in the agent's semi-monthly report, one will be filed at the MLA’s office, and one copy of the lien entry form, one copy of the lien fee receipt and the four part lien release form will be returned to the lien holder.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to file a lien on a semi, you must first obtain a court order (judgment) directing the debtor to pay what is owed, then file a claim with the court and submit proof of the amounts owed, after which the business must answer and explain why the debt is not owed, and after processing, one copy will be attached to the titling documentation with a copy of the lien fee receipt, one copy with the lien fee receipt will be sent to OTC in the agent's semi-monthly report, one will be filed 