{"id": "467", "question": "benefits of hiking as a hobby facts", "gt": "Hiking as a hobby has numerous benefits for both the body and the mind. It is an inexpensive and accessible activity that can be enjoyed by individuals of all fitness levels. Hiking allows people to explore and discover beautiful natural areas, promoting a deeper connection with the environment. It also has positive effects on mental health, reducing stress and anxiety. Additionally, hiking is a cardiovascular activity that can improve overall fitness and reduce the risk of heart disease. Exposure to sunshine during hiking can also increase vitamin D levels in the body. Overall, hiking offers a wide range of benefits for individuals seeking physical and mental well-being.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, benefits of hiking as a hobby facts include: it is inexpensive and easy to start, allowing participation regardless of current fitness level; it promotes mental health by being more varied than gym exercise; exposure to sunshine increases vitamin D levels; it is a cardiovascular activity that reduces heart disease risk and increases overall fitness; and research shows it positively impacts combating stress and anxiety symptoms, as noted by Gregory A. Miller, PhD, president of the American Hiking Society, who states being in nature is ingrained in our DNA.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, benefits of hiking as a hobby facts include: it is inexpensive and easy to start, allowing participation regardless of current fitness level; it promotes mental health by being more varied than gym exercise; exposure to sunshine increases vitamin D levels; it is a cardiovascular activity that reduces heart disease risk and increases overall fitness; and research shows it positively impacts combating stress and anxiety symptoms, as noted by Gregory A. Miller, PhD, president of the Ameri