{"id": "474", "question": "what is the difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, the main differences between refined and unrefined coconut oil are:\n\n1. Source: Refined coconut oil is made from dried coconut fruit, while unrefined coconut oil is made from the flesh of fresh coconuts.\n2. Aroma and flavor: Unrefined coconut oil retains its distinct aroma and flavor, while refined coconut oil loses these qualities during the refining process.\n3. Smoking point: Refined coconut oil has a higher smoking point (450 degrees F) than unrefined coconut oil (350 degrees F), making it more suitable for high-temperature cooking methods like frying.\n\nTherefore, the main differences between refined and unrefined coconut oil are their source, aroma, flavor, and smoking point.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil includes: refined coconut oil is made from dried coconut fruit while unrefined coconut oil is made from the flesh of fresh coconuts; unrefined coconut oil has a distinct aroma and flavor that is lost during refining; refined coconut oil has a higher smoking point of 450 degrees F compared to unrefined coconut oil's 350 degrees F, making it better for high-temperature cooking like frying; and refined coconut oil is deodorized and loses its signature coconut flavor and smell, whereas unrefined oil carries a mild coconut flavor and aroma.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil includes: refined coconut oil is made from dried coconut fruit while unrefined coconut oil is made from the flesh of fresh coconuts; unrefined coconut oil has a distinct aroma and flavor that is lost during refining; refined coconut oil has a higher smoking point of 450 degrees F compared to unrefined coconut oil's 350 