{"id": "479", "question": "change of address u.s. postal service", "gt": "To change your US postal address, you can visit the official website of the U.S. Postal Service, fill out an online form, or contact their call center. The process is fast and versatile, allowing you to notify up to 100 organizations in addition to the USPS. It's important to note that you can also use this feature to have your business mail forwarded to a new address due to a permanent move or temporary relocation. The process involves submitting either an online form or filling out and submitting a physical form at any U.S. Post Office.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, change of address U.S. Postal Service can be done in 1 minute or less through three methods: 1. Visit https://moversguide.usps.com/ and pay a $1 credit or debit card charge for identity validation; 2. Call the USPS Call Center at 1-800-ASK-USPS (1-800-275-8777); 3. Fill out and submit PS Form 3575, available at any U.S. Post Office, mailed to any Post Office, or provided to any Postal Mail Carrier. The service is fast, versatile for notifying up to 100 organizations, and secure with latest encryption technologies.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, change of address U.S. Postal Service can be done in 1 minute or less through three methods: 1. Visit https://moversguide.usps.com/ and pay a $1 credit or debit card charge for identity validation; 2. Call the USPS Call Center at 1-800-ASK-USPS (1-800-275-8777); 3. Fill out and submit PS Form 3575, available at any U.S. Post Office, mailed to any Post Office, or provided to any Postal Mail Carrier. The service is fast, versatile for notifying up to 100 organizations, and secure with latest encryption technologies.", "time_sec": 17.542, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio":