{"id": "480", "question": "change of address u.s. postal service", "gt": "Sure! Based on the given passages, here's a brief answer to the question \"change of address u.s. postal service\":\n\nTo change your address with the U.S. Postal Service, you can visit the USPS website (moversguide.usps.com), call the USPS Call Center (1-800-ASK-USPS), or fill out and submit PS Form 3575 at any U.S. Post Office. You can also use the USPS change of address feature to notify up to 100 organizations, including the Postal Service, with secure encryption technology to protect your data.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, change of address U.S. Postal Service can be done in 1 minute or less through three methods: 1. Visit https://moversguide.usps.com/ and pay a $1 credit or debit card charge for identity validation; 2. Call the USPS Call Center at 1-800-ASK-USPS (1-800-275-8777); 3. Fill out and submit PS Form 3575, available at any U.S. Post Office, mailed to any Post Office, or provided to any Postal Mail Carrier. The service is fast, versatile for notifying up to 100 organizations, and secure with latest encryption technologies.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, change of address U.S. Postal Service can be done in 1 minute or less through three methods: 1. Visit https://moversguide.usps.com/ and pay a $1 credit or debit card charge for identity validation; 2. Call the USPS Call Center at 1-800-ASK-USPS (1-800-275-8777); 3. Fill out and submit PS Form 3575, available at any U.S. Post Office, mailed to any Post Office, or provided to any Postal Mail Carrier. The service is fast, versatile for notifying up to 100 organizations, and secure with latest encryption technologies.", "time_sec": 15.763, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "record_proces