{"id": "489", "question": "how can you tell who liked your tweet", "gt": "You can see who liked your tweets by using tracking websites such as Favotter.net and Favstar.fm. These sites can give you an idea of who is favouriting your tweets. Alternatively, you can also set up notifications on Twitter itself. By going to your account settings and clicking on the notifications link, you can arrange to be notified via email whenever someone likes one of your tweets.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, you can tell who liked your tweet by using Favotter.net or Favstar.fm, which are websites that track favorited tweets and show you who favorited your tweets or the same tweets as you, or by going to Twitter.com, logging in, clicking your name in the upper right corner, selecting Settings, then clicking the blue Notifications link to see notifications of who favorited your tweets.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, you can tell who liked your tweet by using Favotter.net or Favstar.fm, which are websites that track favorited tweets and show you who favorited your tweets or the same tweets as you, or by going to Twitter.com, logging in, clicking your name in the upper right corner, selecting Settings, then clicking the blue Notifications link to see notifications of who favorited your tweets.", "time_sec": 14.786, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 35957, 1408, 1278, 4265, 42679, 1044, 1636, 1710, 5584, 2274, 26648, 2143, 69417, 1536, 2505, 89437, 1360, 1397, 9592, 1505, 89437, 19241, 3175, 1109, 1044, 1799, 1584, 39307, 1455, 6933, 8209, 2770, 88357, 1321, 2629, 1636, 2274, 8209, 2770, 2143, 88357, 1505, 1278, 2879, 88357, 1435, 1636, 1044, 1505, 1536, 4670, 1317, 27464, 2354, 1044, 24850, 1294, 10