{"id": "491", "question": "how can you tell who liked your tweet", "gt": "You can tell who liked your tweet by using websites such as Favotter.net and Favstar.fm, or by going to Twitter.com and logging in with your Twitter username and password. Once logged in, click on your Twitter name, located on the upper right hand corner of your account's Home page, then click on Settings and finally Blue Notifications link at the top of the screen. By setting this feature, you will receive an email notification whenever someone marks one of your tweets as one of their favorites.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, you can tell who liked your tweet by using Favotter.net or Favstar.fm, which are websites that track favorited tweets and show you who favorited your tweets or the same tweets as you, or by going to Twitter.com, logging in, clicking your name in the upper right corner, selecting Settings, then clicking the blue Notifications link to see notifications of who favorited your tweets.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, you can tell who liked your tweet by using Favotter.net or Favstar.fm, which are websites that track favorited tweets and show you who favorited your tweets or the same tweets as you, or by going to Twitter.com, logging in, clicking your name in the upper right corner, selecting Settings, then clicking the blue Notifications link to see notifications of who favorited your tweets.", "time_sec": 9.696, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 35957, 1408, 1278, 4265, 42679, 1044, 1636, 1710, 5584, 2274, 26648, 2143, 69417, 1536, 2505, 89437, 1360, 1397, 9592, 1505, 89437, 19241, 3175, 1109, 1044, 1799, 1584, 39307, 1455, 6933, 8209, 2770, 88357, 1321, 2629, 1636, 2274, 8209, 2770, 2143,