{"id": "508", "question": "what is the difference between sirloin steak and porterhouse steak", "gt": "Porterhouse steaks are cut from further back on the sirloin and contain more of the tenderloin or fillet than sirloin steaks. They are essentially a larger version of the T-Bone steak, carved from a larger portion of the tenderloin. On the other hand, the sirloin steak is a steak cut from the back of the animal, continuing off the short loin from which T-bone, porterhouse, and club steaks are cut. The sirloin is divided into several different types of steak.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the difference between sirloin steak and porterhouse steak is that sirloin steak is cut from the back of the animal, specifically the rear back portion continuing off the short loin, while porterhouse steak is cut from further back on the sirloin and contains a larger portion of the tenderloin or fillet, making it a combination of the fillet and front of the sirloin (short loin) on either side of a T-shaped bone.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the difference between sirloin steak and porterhouse steak is that sirloin steak is cut from the back of the animal, specifically the rear back portion continuing off the short loin, while porterhouse steak is cut from further back on the sirloin and contains a larger portion of the tenderloin or fillet, making it a combination of the fillet and front of the sirloin (short loin) on either side of a T-shaped bone.", "time_sec": 12.496, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 35957, 1408, 1278, 4265, 42679, 1044, 1278, 6592, 2396, 18942, 1906, 1259, 3995, 1489, 1321, 46181, 15454, 3995, 1489, 1395, 1455, 18942, 1906, 1259, 3995, 1489, 1395, 6945, 1562, 1278, 259