{"id": "509", "question": "what is the difference between sirloin steak and porterhouse steak", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the difference between sirloin steak and porterhouse steak is that porterhouse steak is a larger version of T-Bone steak and it contains more of the tenderloin or fillet than T-Bone steak.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the difference between sirloin steak and porterhouse steak is that sirloin steak is cut from the back of the animal, specifically the rear back portion continuing off the short loin, while porterhouse steak is cut from further back on the sirloin and contains a larger portion of the tenderloin or fillet, making it a combination of the fillet and front of the sirloin (short loin) on either side of a T-shaped bone.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the difference between sirloin steak and porterhouse steak is that sirloin steak is cut from the back of the animal, specifically the rear back portion continuing off the short loin, while porterhouse steak is cut from further back on the sirloin and contains a larger portion of the tenderloin or fillet, making it a combination of the fillet and front of the sirloin (short loin) on either side of a T-shaped bone.", "time_sec": 11.727, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 35957, 1408, 1278, 4265, 42679, 1044, 1278, 6592, 2396, 18942, 1906, 1259, 3995, 1489, 1321, 46181, 15454, 3995, 1489, 1395, 1455, 18942, 1906, 1259, 3995, 1489, 1395, 6945, 1562, 1278, 2595, 1307, 1278, 11386, 1044, 13703, 1278, 18268, 2595, 7575, 29357, 2490, 1278, 4958, 25646, 1044, 3016, 46181, 15454, 3995, 1489, 1395, 6945, 1562, 4514, 2595, 1408, 1278, 18942, 1906, 1259, 1321, 8688, 1261, 9039, 7575, 1307, 1278, 44441, 1906,