{"id": "521", "question": "how do raffles work", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's how raffles work:\n\nA raffle is a game of chance where participants buy tickets with a unique number, and a prize is awarded to the holder of the winning ticket drawn at random. In a reverse raffle, the process is similar, but the tickets are numbered from 1 to approximately 55, and tables consist of 20 individuals, constituting one complete ticket at $1000, with two $500 prizes available. In a 50-50 draw, tickets are sold during an event, and the gross proceeds go into a prize pool, with 50% going to the winner of the random draw and the remaining 50% going to a charitable cause.\n\nTherefore, raffles typically involve buying tickets with unique numbers, and a random draw determines the winner, with a percentage of the proceeds often going to a charitable cause.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, raffles work as follows: A reverse raffle is a raffle but backwards where your entry ticket has a number from 1 to approximately 55, tickets cost $50 each, and a table of 20 individuals constitutes one complete ticket at $1000 with two $500 prizes (one for the early bird drawing and one for the first ticket pulled). A 50-50 draw is a raffle held during a single day at an event where tickets are sold to patrons throughout the stadium by roaming staff using handheld electronic mobile devices, with gross proceeds going into a prize pool, 50% of which goes to the winner of the random draw occurring towards the end of the event, and the remaining 50% set aside for a charitable purpose chosen by the sporting club. Additionally, participants have the chance to win $10,000 in cash tip board raffles, which are not included in the ticket price.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, raffles work as follows: A reverse raffle is a raffle but backwards where your entry ticket has a number from 1 to approximately 55, tickets cost $50 each, and a table of 20 individuals constitutes one complete ticket at $1000 with two $500 prizes (one for the early bird drawing and one for the first ticket pulled). A 50-50 draw is a raffle held during a single day at an event where tickets are sold to patrons throughout the stadium by roaming staff using handheld electronic mobile devices, with gross proceeds going into a prize pool, 50% of which goes to the winner of the random draw occurring towards the end of the event, and the remaining 50% set aside for a charitable purpose chosen by the sporting club. Additionally, participants have the chance to win $10,000 in cash tip board raffles, which are not included in the ticket price.", "time_sec": 22.244, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 35957, 1408, 1278, 4265, 42679, 1044, 50665, 2013, 2196, 1435, 9775, 1058, 1349, 16448, 50665, 1282, 1395, 1261, 50665, 1282, 1809, 56972, 2478, 2143, 10505, 30191, 1934, 1261, 2782, 1562, 1032, 1049, 1317, 11267, 1032, 1053, 1053, 1044, 44620, 4362, 1659, 1053, 1048, 2744, 1044, 1321, 1261, 4234, 1307, 1032, 1050, 1048, 8833, 49666, 1925, 7662, 30191, 1513, 1659, 1049, 1048, 1048, 1048, 1454, 2295, 1659, 1053, 1048, 1048, 99941, 1319, 1774, 1394, 1278, 5124, 16409, 20426, 1321, 1925, 1394, 1278, 2158, 30191, 13538, 1577, 1349, 1032, 1053, 1048, 1045, 1053, 1048, 7277, 1395, 1261, 50665, 1282, 6452, 3184, 1261, 4249, 3950, 1513, 1420, 3349, 2478, 44620, 1584, 6981, 1317, 83140, 9743, 1278, 38611, 1536, 1768, 16572, 11212, 2505, 127437, 15356, 11396, 10483, 1044, 1454, 23795, 44015, 4670, 2203, 1261, 41984, 15428, 1044, 1032, 1053, 1048, 1037, 1307, 1799, 12481, 1317, 1278, 24340, 1307, 1278, 6974, 7277, 26454, 8994, 1278, 2362, 1307, 1278, 3349, 1044, 1321, 1278, 11829, 1032, 1053, 1048, 1037, 2016, 27230, 1394, 