{"id": "530", "question": "how does ez pass charges work", "gt": "Sure! Based on the given passages, here is how E-ZPass charging works:\n\nWhen you sign up for E-ZPass, a certain amount is charged to your credit card to establish a balance (specifically, $100 for the EZ-Tag and $25 for the TX-Tag). This balance is used to pay for tolls as you drive through toll lanes. When you drive through a toll booth, the toll tag mounted on your windshield is read by the antennae, and your E-ZPass account is charged the appropriate amount. The amount is deducted from your balance. If your balance falls below a certain threshold ($10 for the TX-Tag), E-ZPass will charge your credit card an additional $100 or $25 to top up your balance.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, how does ez pass charges work: When your vehicle enters a toll lane, the toll tag mounted on your windshield is read by antennas, and your E-ZPass account is charged the proper amount, with feedback displayed electronically; if you do not have a toll tag, the system classifies you as a violator and cameras take photos of your license plate for processing. Additionally, they charge a certain amount from your credit card to establish a balance (it's $100 for the EZ-Tag, $25 for the TX-Tag), deduct the tolls from that balance until the balance goes below a certain value ($10 for the TX-Tag), and then charge your credit card another $100 or $25 to increase your balance.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, how does ez pass charges work: When your vehicle enters a toll lane, the toll tag mounted on your windshield is read by antennas, and your E-ZPass account is charged the proper amount, with feedback displayed electronically; if you do not have a toll tag, the system classifies you as a violator and cameras take photos of your license plate for processing. Additionally, they charge a certain amount from your credit card to establish a balance (it's $100 for the EZ-Tag, $25 for the TX-Tag), deduct the tolls from that balance until the balance goes below a certain value ($10 for the TX-Tag), and then charge your credit card another $100 or $25 to increase your balance.", "time_sec": 13.255, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 35957, 1408, 1278, 4265, 42679, 1044, 2606, 3120, 11317, 2764, 22457, 2196, 1058, 4925, 2143, 11491, 38210, 1261, 44182, 34417, 1044, 1278, 44182, 9066, 19419, 1408, 2143, 12330, 121869, 1395, 3346, 1536, 83722, 1044, 1321, 2143, 1436, 16320, 21889, 5449, 1395, 21080, 1278, 3875, 5647, 1044, 1454, 17887, 15578, 118584, 1059, 1693, 1636, 1653, 1605, 1736, 1261, 44182, 9066, 1044, 1278, 2663, 1845, 16646, 1636, 1435, 1261, 6938, 2412, 1321, 41992, 4069, 17159, 1307, 2143, 28332, 8783, 1394, 8673, 1046, 18011, 1044, 2127, 10162, 1261, 5029, 5647, 1562, 2143, 17959, 6309, 1317, 11925, 1261, 13864, 1319, 1276, 1681, 1659, 1049, 1048, 1048, 1394, 1278, 126518, 8588, 1393, 1044, 1659, 1050, 1053, 1394, 1278, 46330, 8588, 1393, 1574, 8667, 7041, 1278, 44182, 1115, 1562, 1455, 13864, 4570, 1278, 13864, 12481, 5956, 1261, 5029, 2632, 7252, 1049, 1048, 1394, 1278, 46330, 8588, 1393, 1574, 1321, 2430, 10162, 2143, 17959, 6309, 3866, 1659, 1049, 1048, 1048, 1505, 1659, 1050, 1053, 1317, 5597, 2143, 13864, 1046, 11], "logp_list": [-0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0018, -0.7224, -0.0327, -0.0378, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.1215, -0.8617, -0.8389, -0.0015, -0.0027, -0.1273, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0043, -0.0039, -0.683, -0.0, -0.1043, -0.0, -0.0148, -0.0028, -0.0, -0.1128, -0.0, -0.0248, -0.533, -0.5497, -0.0342, -0.0152, -0.0022, -0.0005, -0.0, -0.252, -0.0, -0.0084, -0.0002, -0.001, -0.5764, -1.4571, -0.5563, -0.0224, -0.8412, -0.4749, -0.194, -0.3526, -0.264, -0.8322, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.2519,