{"id": "576", "question": "how to quickly get rid of mice", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here are some ways to quickly get rid of mice:\n\n1. Take immediate action to get rid of mice as soon as possible, as they can quickly take up residence in your home and start nesting (Passage 1).\n2. Seal off all entry points into your home, including holes around pipes and vents, using steel wool to prevent mice from getting back in (Passage 2).\n3. Get rid of any sources of food for mice and rats, as they will quickly take advantage of any food left behind by humans (Passage 3).\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages. The passages do not provide specific instructions on how to quickly get rid of mice once they have entered a home.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to quickly get rid of mice you need to take immediate action as it is a critical step. Mice can very quickly take up residence and start nesting, so act fast. Consider putting steel wool inside entry points like pipes or vents before sealing them off, as steel wool pads prevent mice from using the hole to get back in and add extra protection if mice are persistent. Also, eliminate food sources and seal tiny openings to prevent access, as rodents consume human-discarded food and fit through the tiniest openings.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to quickly get rid of mice you need to take immediate action as it is a critical step. Mice can very quickly take up residence and start nesting, so act fast. Consider putting steel wool inside entry points like pipes or vents before sealing them off, as steel wool pads prevent mice from using the hole to get back in and add extra protection if mice are persistent. Also, eliminate food sources and seal tiny openings to prevent access, as rodents consume human-discarded food and fit through the tiniest openings.", "time_sec": 10.258, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 35957, 1408, 1278, 4265, 42679, 1044, 1317, 10533, 2012, 15515, 1307, 9425, 1636, 2534, 1317, 4069, 20726, 5263, 1435, 1494, 1395, 1261, 10374, 5966, 1046, 80505, 1710, 3435, 10533, 4069, 2015, 31202, 1321, 3030, 100223, 1044, 1878, 2108, 7720, 1046, 24900, 21443, 17698, 74931, 6625, 10505, 5305, 2479, 56593, 1505, 61205, 3066, 48076, 2424, 2490, 1044, 1435, 17698, 74931, 66094, 7495, 9425, 1562, 2505, 1278, 18441, 1317, 2012, 2595, 1294, 1321, 2229, 7185, 11824, 1693, 9425, 1584, 31862, 1046, 9840, 1044, 31924, 6939, 10592, 1321, 28128, 27465, 51837, 1317, 7495, 4731, 1044, 1435, 92466, 45929, 4503, 104437, 36753, 6939, 1321, 8125, 2645, 1278, 1257, 3598, 1372, 51837, 1046, 11], "logp_list": [-0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0007, -0.1667, -0.0004, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.7545, -0.1684, -0.0029, -0.0078, -0.0002, -0.0015, -0.4317, -1.0435, -0.0235, -0.1181, -0.0, -0.0015, -1.2862, -0.0968, -0.0024, -0.3687, -0.0021, -0.0001, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.5234, -0.0019, -0.0, -0.4395, -0.0502, -1.2602, -0.0, -0.0189, -0.8952, -0.1277, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0089, -0.3147, -0.0012, -0.0827, -0.0009, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.0114, -0.0001, -0.0003, -0.0454, -0.1407, -0.0066, -0.6479, -0.0, -0.0129, -0.5786, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0848, -0.234, -0.0185, -0.0013, -0.0024, -0.0, -0.2586, -0.0506, -0.1032, -0.0713, -0.0, -0.3711, -0.3501, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.5389, -1.4246, -0.2644, -0.0389, -0.4151, -0.0002, -0.1811, -0.6303, -0.5022, -0.0, -1.0067, -0.111, -0.2617, -0.2567, -0.1328, -0.0428, -0.269, -0.6706, -0.2861, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.1602, -0.0, -0.6304, -0.1002, 0.0, 0.0, -0.0047, -0.0932, -0.0451], "cumulative_logprob": -19.2608, "norm_logp": -0.1751, "input_len": 486, "output_tokens": 110, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 43.37, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.0, "Status": "success", "GAVIE-Judge": "glm-4.5-flash"}}
{"id": "580", "question": "what do i do if i got my sperrys wet", "gt": "Based on the given passages, if your Sperry shoes get wet, it is recommended to use a leather conditioner to help revitalize the leather and infuse moisture back into it. This is especially important if you wash your shoes with detergent, as it tends to dry out the leather. If you don't have a leather conditioner on hand, you can use a suede bar or leather brush to clean the shoes. It's best to avoid getting light tan Sperry shoes wet, as water might stain them. However, if you do get them wet, using a suede bar or leather brush should help remove any stains.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, if you got your Sperrys wet, you should reassemble the shoes when done, as stated in passage 1. Passage 2 indicates that getting topsiders (Sperrys) wet is not a big deal, especially for regular dark brown ones, though water might stain light tan ones. Passage 3 suggests using a suede bar and leather brush (or a cleaning toothbrush) to handle stains, which are affordable at $5-$10 and worth purchasing for effective cleaning.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, if you got your Sperrys wet, you should reassemble the shoes when done, as stated in passage 1. Passage 2 indicates that getting topsiders (Sperrys) wet is not a big deal, especially for regular dark brown ones, though water might stain light tan ones. Passage 3 suggests using a suede bar and leather brush (or a cleaning toothbrush) to handle stains, which are affordable at $5-$10 and worth purchasing for effective cleaning.", "time_sec": 14.615, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 35957, 1408, 1278, 4265, 42679, 1044, 1693, 1636, 4884, 2143, 86376, 81617, 18258, 1044, 163