{"id": "615", "question": "how to force removal of a printer in devices and printers", "gt": "Passage 2 provides the necessary information to force removal of a printer in devices and printers. You can do this by first clicking on Control Panel, then selecting Hardware and Sound, followed by clicking on Printers. Right-click on the printer you want to remove and click Delete. If you are unable to delete the printer, right-click it again, click Run as administrator, and then click Delete.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to force removal of a printer in devices and printers: Step 2: Remove the printer from the devices list. Step 3: Remove printers and uninstall any Windows print drivers using Windows Devices and Printers. If your printer connects to the computer with a USB cable, disconnect the cable from the printer. Turn the printer off and on again, and make sure that it is in a ready state. Additionally, if you can't delete the printer, right-click it again, click Run as administrator, and then click Delete.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to force removal of a printer in devices and printers: Step 2: Remove the printer from the devices list. Step 3: Remove printers and uninstall any Windows print drivers using Windows Devices and Printers. If your printer connects to the computer with a USB cable, disconnect the cable from the printer. Turn the printer off and on again, and make sure that it is in a ready state. Additionally, if you can't delete the printer, right-click it again, click Run as administrator, and then click Delete.", "time_sec": 13.692, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 35957, 1408, 1278, 4265, 42679, 1044, 1317, 6613, 19084, 1307, 1261, 37376, 1294, 10483, 1321,