{"id": "620", "question": "how has it technology changed the workplace", "gt": "IT technology has significantly changed the workplace in several ways. It has improved efficiency and increased productivity, as it allows for a complete shift in how time is spent in the modern workplace. The continuous evolution of technology also changes how business is conducted and the dynamics of the workplace. Over the last 10 to 15 years, technology has drastically changed attitudes and processes in the workplace. Technology has also dramatically reshaped the average American workplace, allowing employees to interact with a global market and take work on the road.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, technology has changed the workplace in several ways: 1. It has increased efficiency and productivity by shifting how time is spent in the workplace. 2. Over the last 10 to 15 years, it has drastically changed workplace attitudes and processes. 3. It has enabled employees to interact with a global market and work remotely, as noted in the modern workplace evolution. 4. The workplace environment has transformed from the traditional office setting of yesteryear due to rapid technological advancement.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, technology has changed the workplace in several ways: 1. It has increased efficiency and productivity by shifting how time is spent in the workplace. 2. Over the last 10 to 15 years, it has drastically changed workplace attitudes and processes. 3. It has enabled employees to interact with a global market and work remotely, as noted in the modern workplace evolution. 4. The workplace environment has transformed from the traditional office setting of yesteryear due to rapid technological advancement.", "time_sec": 14.559, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, 