{"id": "625", "question": "how has it technology changed the workplace", "gt": "Based on the given passages, technology has changed the workplace in several ways, including:\n\n1. Increased efficiency and productivity: Technology has enabled automation of many tasks, allowing employees to focus on more complex and creative work, leading to increased productivity.\n2. Changes in workplace dynamics: Technology has transformed the way people communicate and collaborate in the workplace, enabling remote work and virtual teams.\n3. Rapid advancements: Technology has rapidly advanced in recent years, allowing employees to access new tools and resources, and adapt to changing market conditions.\n4. Global connectivity: Technology has enabled employees to interact with a global market and work remotely, allowing for greater flexibility and mobility.\n\nTherefore, technology has had a significant impact on the modern workplace, transforming the way people work, communicate, and collaborate.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, technology has changed the workplace in several ways: 1. It has increased efficiency and productivity by shifting how time is spent in the workplace. 2. Over the last 10 to 15 years, it has drastically changed workplace attitudes and processes. 3. It has enabled employees to interact with a global market and work remotely, as noted in the modern workplace evolution. 4. The workplace environment has transformed from the traditional office setting of yesteryear due to rapid technological advancement.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, technology has changed the workplace in several ways: 1. It has increased efficiency and productivity by shifting how time is spent in the workplace. 2. Over the last 10 to 15 years, it has drastically changed workplace attitudes and processes. 3. It has enabled employees to interact with a global marke