{"id": "645", "question": "how to plant a potato that has sprouted", "gt": "To plant a sprouted potato, cut it into chunks with two or three eyes each. Place the potato chunks on a tray or cookie sheet and let them dry out overnight. Dig a trench about 4 inches wide and 6 to 8 inches deep in a prepared planting area. Place the sprouted or eye side of the potato chunks facing up, separating each chunk by about 6 to 8 inches. Cover the potatoes with a layer of compost and then replace the dirt on top. Water the potatoes thoroughly and continue watering regularly when the soil is dry to the touch. Add a 4-inch layer of mulch around the plants to keep the soil cool and maintain moisture.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to plant a sprouted potato: Cut large, sprouted potatoes into chunks with two or three eyes each, using a sharp knife, being careful to not break the long sprouts, or cut your potatoes into cubes, about 1 to 2 inches on each side, leaving a sprout on each cube. Place the cubes into the bottom of a trench about 4 inches wide and 6 to 8 inches deep, separating each cube from the other by about 6 to 8 inches, with the sprouted or eye side facing up, then cover the potatoes with a layer of compost and replace the dirt on top.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to plant a sprouted potato: Cut large, sprouted potatoes into chunks with two or three eyes each, using a sharp knife, being careful to not break the long sprouts, or cut your potatoes into cubes, about 1 to 2 inches on each side, leaving a sprout on each cube. Place the cubes into the bottom of a trench about 4 inches wide and 6 to 8 inches deep, separating each cube from the other by about 6 to 8 inches, with the sprouted or eye side facing up, then cover the potatoes with a layer of compost and replace the dirt on top.", "time_sec": 16.953, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transform