{"id": "648", "question": "color of urin meaning", "gt": "The color of urine can indicate various health conditions. Normal urine is typically pale yellow, due to the pigment urochrome. If kidney diseases are present, the filtration and re-absorption stages of urine production may be malfunctioning, altering this pale color. Red urine is typically a sign of blood in the urine, which can indicate serious conditions like infections or cancer. Deep purple urine is an identifying characteristic of porphyria, a rare, inherited disorder of red blood cells. Foods and medications can also affect urine color, with beets, berries, and fava beans being among the most likely to cause changes.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the color of urine meaning is that seeing red urine typically indicates blood in the urine, which can signify serious conditions like infection or cancer; deep purple urine is an identifying characteristic of porphyria, a rare inherited disorder of red blood cells; and the normal color of urine is pale yellow due to the pigment urochrome, though this can be altered in kidney diseases.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the color of urine meaning is that seeing red urine typically indicates blood in the urine, which can signify serious conditions like infection or cancer; deep purple urine is an identifying characteristic of porphyria, a rare inherited disorder of red blood cells; and the normal color of urine is pale yellow due to the pigment urochrome, though this can be altered in kidney diseases.", "time_sec": 8.697, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 35957, 1408, 1278, 4265, 42679, 1044, 1278, 4558, 1307, 35180, 10138, 1395, 1455, 17209, 4804, 35180, 12837, 13709, 6517, 12