{"id": "662", "question": "vinegar uses for dogs", "gt": "Sure, I can answer your question based on the given passages. Here are some uses for vinegar for dogs:\n\n1. Coat and skin health: Mixing vinegar with water and using it as a final rinse can help to rejuvenate your dog's coat and balance their skin pH levels, according to Passage 1.\n2. Flea control: Vinegar can be used to repel fleas and remove them from your dog's coat, as mentioned in Passage 2.\n3. Itchy ears: Diluted vinegar can be used to soothe itchy ears, as stated in Passage 3.\n\nI hope this helps! Let me know if you have any further questions or if there's anything else I can assist you with.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, vinegar uses for dogs include: mixing 1 cup of vinegar with 2-4 cups of water for a final rinse to rejuvenate the coat and balance skin pH levels; spraying vinegar full-strength on the dog's coat to normalize skin pH balance; using a diluted solution of apple cider vinegar with 50 percent water to soothe itchy ears by applying with a cotton swab or gauze pad; cleaning dog's ears with ACV; spraying the coat to repel fleas; bathing in an ACV-soap mixture to fight fleas; using a flea comb to remove fleas; and rinsing the dog.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, vinegar uses for dogs include: mixing 1 cup of vinegar with 2-4 cups of water for a final rinse to rejuvenate the coat and balance skin pH levels; spraying vinegar full-strength on the dog's coat to normalize skin pH balance; using a diluted solution of apple cider vinegar with 50 percent water to soothe itchy ears by applying with a cotton swab or gauze pad; cleaning dog's ears with ACV; spraying the coat to repel fleas; bathing in an ACV-soap mixture to fight fleas; using a flea comb to remove fleas; and rinsing the dog.", "time_sec": 17.826, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote