{"id": "666", "question": "what happens when you breath in and out", "gt": "When you breathe in, your diaphragm contracts and pulls downwards, expanding the chest cavity. The intercostal muscles between the ribs also contract to expand the ribcage. Pressure inside the chest is reduced, causing air to be sucked into the lungs. On the other hand, when you breathe out, your diaphragm relaxes and moves upward into the chest cavity, reducing the space in the chest cavity. Air rich in carbon dioxide is then forced out of the lungs and windpipe. Breathing out does not require any effort from your body unless you have a lung disease or are doing physical activity.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, when you breathe out, your diaphragm relaxes and moves upward into the chest cavity while the intercostal muscles between the ribs relax to reduce the space in the chest cavity, forcing air rich in carbon dioxide out of your lungs, windpipe, and then out of your nose or mouth, which requires no effort unless you have a lung disease or are doing physical activity; when you breathe in, the intercostal muscles contract to expand the ribcage, the diaphragm contracts pulling downwards to increase the volume of the chest, lowering the pressure inside the chest and sucking air into the lungs, and outside air pushes into your windpipe (trachea) into your lungs, with a hole in the chest wall allowing air to enter through that hole, causing air to gather around the lung and collapse it when there is a large amount of air around the outside of the lung preventing expansion.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, when you breathe out, your diaphragm relaxes and moves upward into the chest cavity while the intercostal muscles between the ribs relax to reduce the space in the chest cavity, forcing air rich in carbon dioxide out of your lungs, windpipe, and then out of your nose or mouth, which requires no effort unless you have a lung disease or are doing physical activity; when you breathe in, the intercostal muscles contract to expand the ribcage, the diaphragm contracts pulling downwards to increase the volume of the chest, lowering the pressure inside the chest and sucking air into the lungs, and outside air pushes into your windpipe (trachea) into your lungs, with a hole in the chest wall allowing air to enter through that hole, causing air to gather around the lung and collapse it when there is a large amount of air around the outside of the lung preventing expansion.", "time_sec": 25.424, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 35957, 1408, 1278, 4265, 42679, 1044, 2200, 1636, 56336, 1848, 1044, 2143, 82410, 18110, 1264, 1321, 20183, 40022, 2203, 1278, 15448, 27927, 3016, 1278, 35325, 80715, 24812, 2396, 1278, 63484, 18110, 1317, 9980, 1278, 5702, 1294, 1278, 15448, 27927, 1044, 37630, 4864, 12478, 1294, 10006, 42812, 1848, 1307, 2143, 40707, 1044, 12330, 42712, 1044, 1321, 2430, 1848, 1307, 2143, 24917, 1505, 11504, 1044, 1799, 10867, 1836, 8267, 15388, 1636, 1736, 1261, 12025, 6137, 1505, 1584, 6965, 8137, 5177, 1059, 2200, 1636, 56336, 1294, 1044, 1278, 35325, 80715, 24812, 8633, 1317, 10959, 1278, 16120, 1099, 1541, 1044, 1278, 82410, 36010, 29886, 3151, 4969, 1317, 5597, 1278, 8167, 1307, 1278, 15448, 1044, 53943, 1278, 6909, 6625, 1278, 15448, 1321, 107492, 4864, 2203, 1278, 40707, 1044, 1321, 7805, 4864, 77697, 2203, 2143, 12330, 42712, 1319, 1116, 30630, 1097, 1041, 2203, 2143, 40707, 1044, 1454, 1261, 18441, 1294, 1278, 15448, 8751, 15249, 4864, 1317, 6889, 2645, 1455, 18441, 1044, 16312, 4864, 1317, 15646, 3879, 1278, 12025, 1321, 31098, 1494, 2200, 2156, 1395, 1261, 4329, 5647, 1307, 4864, 3879, 1278, 7805, 1307, 1278, 12025, 29449, 15898, 1046, 11], "logp_list": [-0