{"id": "695", "question": "How do you make ice cream", "gt": "To make ice cream, you start by stirring sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until the sugar has dissolved. Heat just until the mix is hot and a small ring of foam appears around the edge. Next, transfer the cream mixture to a pourable container such as a large measuring cup and stir in vanilla extract. Chill the mix thoroughly, for at least 2 hours. Once chilled, pour the cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker, turn on the machine, and churn according to manufacturer's directions for 20 to 25 minutes. When the ice cream is softly frozen, you can serve it immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, 1 Pour cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker, turn on the machine, and churn according to manufacturer's directions, 20 to 25 minutes. 2 When ice cream is softly frozen, serve immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place in freezer to ripen, 2 to 3 hours. 1 Stir sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until sugar has dissolved. 2 Heat just until mix is hot and a small ring of foam appears around the edge. 3 Transfer cream mixture to a pourable container such as a large measuring cup. 4 Stir in vanilla extract and chill mix thoroughly, at least 2 hours. 3 Mix your base. It's easy to make a wide variety of ice cream flavors by starting with a good vanilla ice cream base. Cream-based ice cream is a bit icier and lighter than custard-based ice cream. This recipe will make one quart of ice cream, so double it if you want more.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, 1 Pour cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker, turn on the machine, and churn according to manufacturer's directions, 20 to 25 minutes. 2 When ice cream is softly frozen, serve immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place in freezer to ripen, 2 to 3 hours. 1 Stir sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until sugar has dissolved. 2 Heat just until mix is hot and a small ring of foam appears around the edge. 3 Transfer cream mixture to a pourable container such as a large measuring cup. 4 Stir in vanilla extract and chill mix thoroughly, at least 2 hours. 3 Mix your base. It's easy to make a wide variety of ice cream flavors by starting with a good vanilla ice cream base. Cream-based ice cream is a bit icier and lighter than custard-based ice cream. This recipe will make one quart of ice cream, so double it if you want more.", "time_sec": 32.774, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 35957, 1408, 1278, 4265, 42679, 1044, 1032, 1049, 10108, 13074, 16254, 38423, 11986, 2203, 1420, 16254, 38423, 69947, 1044, 3884, 1408, 1278, 8832, 1044, 1321, 121978, 5138, 1317, 24705, 1681, 22428, 1044, 1032, 1050, 1048, 1317, 1032, 1050, 1053, 7334, 1046, 1032, 1050, 4925, 16254, 38423, 1395, 45118, 32362, 1044, 11584, 10912, 1505, 3535, 1261, 13079, 1307, 17985, 30711, 7655, 1408, 1278, 16254, 38423, 1321, 3535, 1294, 5370, 5176, 1317, 21033, 1262, 1044, 1032, 1050, 1317, 1032, 1051, 7700, 1046, 1032, 1049, 49821, 24224, 1044, 38423, 1044, 1321, 21842, 2203, 1261, 52812, 6318, 2136, 4253, 9374, 4570, 24224, 1934, 28862, 1046, 1032, 1050, 39253, 2586, 4570, 11986, 1395, 8480, 1321, 1261, 3709, 10749, 1307, 50842, 10249, 3879, 1278, 10314, 1046, 1032, 1051, 44250, 38423, 13810, 1317, 1261, 6212, 30831, 11024, 2516, 1435, 1261, 4329, 21747, 19339, 1046, 1032, 1052, 49821, 1294, 99927, 9041, 1321, 76844, 11986, 43850, 1044, 1513, 4403, 1032, 1050, 7700, 1046, 1032, 1051, 28978, 2143, 4469, 1046, 2157, 1681, 9517, 1317, 3180, 