{"id": "699", "question": "How do you make ice cream", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is how you can make ice cream:\n\n1. Pour cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker and turn on the machine, following the manufacturer's instructions (passage 1).\n2. Stir sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until sugar has dissolved, then heat just until a small ring of foam appears around the edge (passage 2).\n3. Transfer the cream mixture to a pourable container and stir in vanilla extract before chilling the mix thoroughly for at least 2 hours (passage 2).\n4. Once the ice cream base is ready, pour it into the ice cream maker and churn according to the manufacturer's instructions (passage 1).\n5. When the ice cream is softly frozen, serve immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours (passage 1).\n\nNote that the passages do not provide a specific recipe for making ice cream, but rather provide general steps and tips for making ice cream using an ice cream maker.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, 1 Pour cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker, turn on the machine, and churn according to manufacturer's directions, 20 to 25 minutes. 2 When ice cream is softly frozen, serve immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place in freezer to ripen, 2 to 3 hours. 1 Stir sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until sugar has dissolved. 2 Heat just until mix is hot and a small ring of foam appears around the edge. 3 Transfer cream mixture to a pourable container such as a large measuring cup. 4 Stir in vanilla extract and chill mix thoroughly, at least 2 hours. 3 Mix your base. It's easy to make a wide variety of ice cream flavors by starting with a good vanilla ice cream base. Cream-based ice cream is a bit icier and lighter than custard-based ice cream. This recipe will make one quart of ice cream, so double it if you want more.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, 1 Pour cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker, turn on the machine, and churn according to manufacturer's directions, 20 to 25 minutes. 2 When ice cream is softly frozen, serve immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place in freezer to ripen, 2 to 3 hours. 1 Stir sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until sugar has dissolved. 2 Heat just until mix is hot and a small ring of foam appears around the edge. 3 Transfer cream mixture to a pourable container such as a large measuring cup. 4 Stir in vanilla extract and chill mix thoroughly, at least 2 hours. 3 Mix your base. It's easy to make a wide variety of ice cream flavors by starting with a good vanilla ice cream base. Cream-based ice cream is a bit icier and lighter than custard-based ice cream. This recipe will make one quart of ice cream, so double it if you want more.", "time_sec": 32.155, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 35957, 1408, 1278, 4265, 42679, 1044, 1032, 1049, 10108, 13074, 16254, 38423, 11986, 2203, 1420, 16254, 38423, 69947, 1044, 3884, 1408, 1278, 8832, 1044, 1321, 121978, 5138, 1317, 24705, 1681, 22428, 1044, 1032, 1050, 1048, 1317, 1032, 1050, 1053, 7334, 1046, 1032, 1050, 4925, 16254, 38423, 1395, 45118, 32362, 1044, 11584, 10912, 1505, 3535, 1261, 13079, 1307, 17985, 30711, 7655, 1408, 1278, 16254, 38423, 1321, 3535, 1294, 5370, 5176, 1317, 21033, 1262, 1044, 1032, 1050, 1317, 1032, 1051, 7700, 1046, 1032, 1049, 49821, 24224, 1044, 38423, 1044, 1321, 21842, 2203, 1261, 52812, 6318, 2136, 4253, 9374, 4570, 24224, 1934, 28862, 1046, 1032, 1050, 39253, 2586, 4570, 11986, 1395, 8480, 1321, 1261, 3709, 10749, 1307, 50842, 10249, 3879