{"id": "701", "question": "what do children learn with water play", "gt": "Children learn various skills and concepts through water play. It aids in the development of gross motor skills as they engage in activities like running through sprinklers or filling and pouring water from buckets. Water play also facilitates academic learning in areas such as science and math. Children learn about the concept of floating and sinking, and understand that different objects have different buoyancies. In math, they learn about measurement by determining the amount of water that fits into a bucket, and concepts of more and less by comparing water levels in different buckets. Water play also promotes creativity, allowing children to use their imagination.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, children learn about gross motor skills through activities like running through sprinklers or filling and pouring buckets, academic concepts such as science (floating and sinking) and math (measuring water amounts), and creativity through imaginative play.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, children learn about gross motor skills through activities like running through sprinklers or filling and pouring buckets, academic concepts such as science (floating and sinking) and math (measuring water amounts), and creativity through imaginative play.", "time_sec": 7.265, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 35957, 1408, 1278, 4265, 42679, 1044, 4974, 8178, 2314, 23795, 9085, 14627, 2645, 9216, 2479, 7523, 2645, 95228, 18099, 1505, 31073, 1321, 88760, 107367, 1044, 19647, 20975, 2516, 1435, 12470, 1319, 1102, 52694, 1321, 80483, 1041, 1321, 20267, 1319, 1804, 121434, 4180, 19491, 1574, 1321, 57432, 2645, 38841, 2277, 3354, 104