{"id": "705", "question": "what do children learn with water play", "gt": "Based on the given passages, children learn the following through water play:\n\n1. Gross motor skills: Running, pouring, and manipulating water helps develop fine and gross motor skills. (Passage 1)\n2. Science concepts: Floating and sinking, measurement, and experimentation with different objects in water. (Passage 1)\n3. Creativity and imagination: Water play encourages children to use their imagination and engage in pretend play. (Passage 1)\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages. The passages do not mention any other specific academic learning outcomes beyond gross motor skills, science concepts, and creativity.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, children learn about gross motor skills through activities like running through sprinklers or filling and pouring buckets, academic concepts such as science (floating and sinking) and math (measuring water amounts), and creativity through imaginative play.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, children learn about gross motor skills through activities like running through sprinklers or filling and pouring buckets, academic concepts such as science (floating and sinking) and math (measuring water amounts), and creativity through imaginative play.", "time_sec": 10.214, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 35957, 1408, 1278, 4265, 42679, 1044, 4974, 8178, 2314, 23795, 9085, 14627, 2645, 9216, 2479, 7523, 2645, 95228, 18099, 1505, 31073, 1321, 88760, 107367, 1044, 19647, 20975, 2516, 1435, 12470, 1319, 1102, 52694, 1321, 80483, 1041, 1321, 20267, 1319, 1804, 121434, 4180, 19491, 1574, 1321, 57432, 2645, 38841, 2277, 3354, 1046, 11], "logp_list": [0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -