{"id": "709", "question": "what do the colors of the tennessee flag mean", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is the answer to the question:\n\nThe colors of the Tennessee flag have the following meanings:\n\n* White represents purity\n* Blue represents patriotism\n* Red represents the willingness to shed blood during warfare\n\nThe three white stars on the flag represent the three grand divisions of Tennessee: East, Middle, and West. The blue field with the white stars is meant to symbolize the three divisions bound together as one.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the colors of the Tennessee flag have the following meanings: White symbolizes purity, blue stands for the patriotism of the people of Tennessee, and red stands for the readiness of the people to shed blood during warfare. These colors are the national colors of the US.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the colors of the Tennessee flag have the following meanings: White symbolizes purity, blue stands for the patriotism of the people of Tennessee, and red stands for the readiness of the people to shed blood during warfare. These colors are the national colors of the US.", "time_sec": 6.876, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 35957, 1408, 1278, 4265, 42679, 1044, 1278, 18666, 1307, 1278, 34075, 12585, 1736, 1278, 3629, 52542, 1058, 10330, 9501, 9357, 52210, 1044, 10991, 23737, 1394, 1278, 84320, 2578, 1307, 1278, 3306, 1307, 34075, 1044, 1321, 4804, 23737, 1394, 1278, 91711, 1307, 1278, 3306, 1317, 42878, 6517, 3184, 56184, 1046, 4634, 18666, 1584, 1278, 6168, 18666, 1307, 1278, 3825, 1046, 11], "logp_list": [0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.001, -0.3432, -0.0105, -0.0065, -0.0, -0.0003, -0.3869, -0.4385, -0.43