{"id": "735", "question": "what is the difference between sms and mms", "gt": "SMS stands for Short Message Service, commonly referred to as a text message, and allows you to send a text message of up to 160 characters to another device. MMS, which stands for Multimedia Messaging Service, is an evolution of SMS. It allows you to send messages that include pictures, video, or audio content to another device. MMS messages can carry a larger size of content up to 300KB. SMS is restricted to sending text-only messages, whereas MMS allows a combination of text, pictures, sounds, and videos.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, SMS only allows sending text messages, while MMS allows sending pictures, sounds, videos, text, or any combination of these four types of content. SMS messages are limited to 160 characters and are split into multiple parts if longer, whereas MMS messages can carry larger content sizes up to 300KB and support multimedia formats like WAV, JPEG, and GIF. SMS is a text-only service, whereas MMS is an evolution of SMS that supports multimedia content.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, SMS only allows sending text messages, while MMS allows sending pictures, sounds, videos, text, or any combination of these four types of content. SMS messages are limited to 160 characters and are split into multiple parts if longer, whereas MMS messages can carry larger content sizes up to 300KB and support multimedia formats like WAV, JPEG, and GIF. SMS is a text-only service, whereas MMS is an evolution of SMS that supports multimedia content.", "time_sec": 16.54, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 35957, 1408, 1278, 4265, 42679, 1044, 54030, 2342, 9985, 20234, 3403, 14193, 1044, 3016, 1373