{"id": "737", "question": "what is the difference between sms and mms", "gt": "Based on the given passages, SMS stands for Short Message Service and allows you to send a message of up to 160 characters to another device. In contrast, MMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) allows you to send a message including pictures, videos, sounds, text, or any combination of the four. The content of an MMS message has a maximum size of 300KB in extensions of WAV, JPEG, GIF, etc.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, SMS only allows sending text messages, while MMS allows sending pictures, sounds, videos, text, or any combination of these four types of content. SMS messages are limited to 160 characters and are split into multiple parts if longer, whereas MMS messages can carry larger content sizes up to 300KB and support multimedia formats like WAV, JPEG, and GIF. SMS is a text-only service, whereas MMS is an evolution of SMS that supports multimedia content.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_model_nemotron", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, SMS only allows sending text messages, while MMS allows sending pictures, sounds, videos, text, or any combination of these four types of content. SMS messages are limited to 160 characters and are split into multiple parts if longer, whereas MMS messages can carry larger content sizes up to 300KB and support multimedia formats like WAV, JPEG, and GIF. SMS is a text-only service, whereas MMS is an evolution of SMS that supports multimedia content.", "time_sec": 11.375, "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "media": {"video": false, "audio": false, "image": false}}, "record_process": true, "token_ids": [1010, 35957, 1408, 1278, 4265, 42679, 1044, 54030, 2342, 9985, 20234, 3403, 14193, 1044, 3016, 1373, 7985, 9985, 20234, 23874, 1044, 18267, 1044, 26612, 1044, 3403, 1044, 1505, 2258, 9943, 1307, 2576, 3946, 6413, 1307, 4701